rfolgslogik – du wirst für Output belohnt)</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Skalierbare Perspektive</strong>: Option auf Übernahme ins Trainee-Programm</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Remote möglich</strong> – eigenverantwortlich statt “nach Uhr”</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Team mit Performance-Kultur</strong>: klare Kommunikation, klare Ergebnisse</p></li></ul><br /><br /><h3>Nichts für dich, wenn…</h3><ul><li><p>du einen typischen Werkstudentenjob mit “ein paar Stunden nebenbei” suchst</p></li><li><p>du Telefon/Terminaufbau vermeiden willst</p></li><li><p>dein Deutsch unter <strong>C1</strong> liegt</p></li><li><p>du lieber Sicherheit als Entwicklung priorisierst</p></li></ul><p style=";"></p><h3>Muss</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Immatrikuliert</strong> (Uni/FH)</p></li><li><p><strong>Deutsch mindestens C1</strong> (mündlich &amp; schriftlich)</p></li><li><p>Kommunikationsstärke, Verbindlichkeit, Zuverlässigkeit</p></li><li><p>Eigeninitiative und strukturierte Arbeitsweise</p></li><li><p>Lust auf Leistung und messbare Ergebnisse</p></li></ul><p style=";"></p><h3>Wunsch</h3><ul><li><p><span style="color: #000000">Erste Erfahrung in Vertrieb, Service, Beratung, Sport-/Leistungskultur</span></p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/kevin-kehr/werkstudent-finance-beratung-unternehmerisch-leistungsbasiert-hamburg-367022","tags":["Finance","high school or equivalent"],"job_types":["Full-time permanent","entry"],"location":"Hamburg","created_at":1793953211},{"slug":"full-stack-engineer-data-infrastructure-ai-berlin-440195","company_name":"Agent F GmbH","title":"Full-Stack Engineer - Data, Infrastructure & AI","description":"<h3><strong>About Agent F</strong></h3><p>Agent F is building an autonomous finance function: software that takes on the work of keeping a company’s finances in order. That means bringing information together from different systems, recording transactions correctly, preparing useful reports, and helping people understand what needs their attention.</p><p>Today, much of this work depends on spreadsheets, repeated data entry and people checking one system against another. Our ambition is to make that work increasingly automatic, while keeping every number explainable and every consequential action under clear control.</p><p>We are building towards a complete business management system for growing companies. These founding roles will shape both the product and the way we build it.</p><h3><strong>About the role</strong></h3><p>You will be a full-stack engineer, shipping customer features across the interface, application services and database. Your particular strength will be the data and infrastructure that make those features dependable: how records are stored, how imports and background jobs run, and how information moves between Agent F and a customer’s other tools. You will help build and operate the whole product, with deeper ownership of this foundation.</p><p>This is hands-on full-stack engineering. A typical piece of work could involve extending a data model, implementing an application service, connecting it to a screen, testing it against a real database and following the release into production. You will also investigate slow reports, failed imports and jobs that stop halfway through, then improve the system so it handles those situations reliably.</p><p>That foundation also supports our AI work. As we add document extraction, connected customer knowledge and software that takes actions for customers, you will build the services and data access those features need. The immediate priority is dependable software that customers can use, with more capable automation developed around specific tasks.</p><h3><strong>What you will build and improve</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Application services and customer features.</strong> Build the logic and application programming interfaces (APIs) that connect records, business rules and screens. Take features through implementation, testing, release and production support.</p></li><li><p><strong>The database foundation.</strong> Design clear data models, enforce relationships and transaction boundaries, and improve slow queries. Manage schema changes through reviewed migrations, preserve financial history and keep each customer’s data isolated.</p></li><li><p><strong>Imports and integrations.</strong> Connect accounting tools, business systems and spreadsheets to a consistent model. Validate incoming records, handle changing source formats, and check that imported totals and reports agree with the source.</p></li><li><p><strong>Reliable background processing.</strong> Build scheduled jobs and workers that process work outside a user request. Handle retries without creating duplicates, resume interrupted runs, and make progress and failures visible to the team.</p></li><li><p><strong>Performance and recovery.</strong> Diagnose expensive queries, processing bottlenecks and partial failures. Test changes against real databases, plan for growing workloads, and build procedures to recover processing safely with the platform engineer.</p></li><li><p><strong>Practical AI automation.</strong> Add features such as extracting invoice fields or preparing an order from approved business data. Give models access through controlled services, check the result and require approval where needed. Develop connected customer knowledge when a feature needs those relationships, and measure whether it improves the result.</p></li></ul><p>For example, a large customer import stops halfway through and the same records arrive again on the next run. You would make processing resume safely, prevent duplicate records, verify the resulting totals and expose the job’s status in the product. You would also investigate whether database queries or worker capacity caused the failure and ship the necessary fix.</p><h3><strong>What you bring</strong></h3><p>You have seven or more years of software engineering experience, including substantial ownership of production applications and data systems. You have designed relational data models, built services and processing pipelines, and stayed responsible for them after release. You are comfortable delivering across the stack and using AI tools in your daily work.</p><p>You can explain how you diagnosed a slow query, recovered a failed job or shipped a database change safely. You understand what happens when two requests arrive at once, a dependency becomes unavailable or a process restarts halfway through its work. You can follow a problem from a source record through the application to the result a customer sees.</p><h3><strong>Core experience</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Full-stack development with TypeScript, Node.js, React and PostgreSQL, or closely comparable technologies.</p></li><li><p>Relational data modelling, SQL, query optimisation, indexes, transactions and reviewed database migrations.</p></li><li><p>Application services and APIs, including permissions, validation and handling concurrent requests.</p></li><li><p>Data imports, integrations and background jobs, including queues, safe retries and recovery from partial failures.</p></li><li><p>Production debugging, service monitoring and performance work on systems used by real customers.</p></li><li><p>Automated tests against real databases and other service dependencies.</p></li><li><p>Practical use of AI in software, with an understanding of how to check outputs and control access to customer data.</p></li><li><p>Daily use of AI coding agents, with direct responsibility for code review and verification.</p></li><li><p>A computer science or computer engineering degree, or equivalent practical depth.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Useful additional experience</strong></h3><p>Financial or operational systems where correctness and traceability matter; larger data migrations; cloud storage and container-based workloads. Experience putting document extraction or features using large language models (LLMs) into production would be valuable. Knowledge graphs, which connect related company records, and privately hosted or adapted models are useful as we develop that part of the product.</p><h3><strong>What early progress could look like</strong></h3><p>In your first months, you would take ownership of an existing service or data flow, understand how it runs in production and ship a customer-facing improvement through it. You would address a concrete reliability or performance problem, such as a slow report, a fragile integration or a job that cannot recover cleanly after interruption.</p><p>We would look for working features, faster and more predictable processing, fewer failed or manually repaired jobs, and useful tests and monitoring. An early automation feature could follow where the data and services are ready and its benefit can be measured.</p><h3><strong>Operational excellence and customer commitments</strong></h3><p>You take pride in a dependable application backbone: processing completes, records reconcile and customers can trust the results. When a job fails or figures disagree, you take ownership of the investigation and recovery. Missing transactions, duplicate entries or unexplained balance differences can be financial emergencies even while every service appears available. You assess the impact, contain affected processing, trace the cause and verify the repaired result before treating the incident as resolved.</p><p>Customer commitments shape how we work. You are willing to interrupt planned work, respond promptly and stay engaged when an urgent issue puts a service-level agreement (SLA), onboarding commitment or financial deadline at risk. That requires flexibility beyond normal working hours as part of agreed on-call coverage and coordinated incident response. You keep people informed and see the issue through to a verified recovery or an explicit handover. Afterwards, you improve the system so the same emergency becomes less likely.</p><h3><strong>How you will work</strong></h3><p>This is a senior founding role in a small team. You will own the application and data infrastructure for your work, and carry a full share of customer feature delivery. You will collaborate across infrastructure, operations and product design to deliver complete customer outcomes. You will use coding agents to implement changes and remain responsible for reviewing, testing and operating the result.</p><p>Everyone shares responsibility for the whole product and the customer outcome. You will pick up the most important work or whatever is on fire, including tasks outside your specialty. You take initiative, bring in the right expertise and stay involved until the problem is resolved. Customer impact and urgency determine where you focus.</p><p>The role is full-time and in-person in Berlin. German is not required.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/agent-f-gmbh/full-stack-engineer-data-infrastructure-ai-berlin-440195","tags":["Software Development"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793952064},{"slug":"technical-project-manager-berlin-152252","company_name":"DARK MATTER gGmbH","title":"Technical Project Manager (m/w/d)","description":"<p>DARK MATTER redefines the interfaces between technology, creativity and interaction in order to create space for personal sensory experiences.</p><p>DARK MATTER is an exhibition made of expansive light installations within a converted factory. The exhibition introduces new and technical concepts, most of which will be made visible to the public for the very first time.</p><h2>YOUR TASKS:</h2><ul><li><p>Planning, coordination, and management of technical development projects in the field of art for DARK MATTER. From the concept phase through to implementation, while ensuring compliance with quality, timeline, and budget requirements.</p></li><li><p>Active involvement in mechanical design and development, including individual components, assemblies, and custom-built constructions.</p></li><li><p>Development and implementation of technical solutions for kinetic installations, moving structures, and mechanically complex lighting and media systems.</p></li><li><p>Close collaboration with development, production, procurement, and other internal and external specialist departments to ensure successful project implementation.</p></li><li><p>Working with mechanical drive systems, automation technology, and interfaces to control systems to support the integration of complex art installations.</p></li><li><p>Identification and resolution of technical challenges through troubleshooting, root cause analysis, as well as testing and validation procedures.</p></li><li><p>Technical support during manufacturing, assembly, installation, and commissioning of the art installations at DARK MATTER to ensure the successful implementation of the developed solutions</p></li><li><p>Creation and review of technical drawings, bills of materials (BOMs), specifications, and other technical documentation.</p></li></ul><h2>YOU BRING:</h2><ul><li><p>A degree in Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related technical field, or an equivalent technical qualification.</p></li><li><p>Several years of experience in mechanical engineering, technical development, or special-purpose machinery (Sondermaschinenbau).</p></li><li><p>Experience managing technical projects or taking ownership of complex engineering work packages.</p></li><li><p>Strong hands-on mechanical design and problem-solving skills, with experience developing components and assemblies.</p></li><li><p>Understanding of mechanical drive systems, automation, control systems, and the integration of moving mechanical structures.</p></li><li><p>Experience working with CAD software and preparing technical drawings, BOMs, and engineering documentation.</p></li><li><p>Practical experience supporting manufacturing, assembly, testing, or commissioning.</p></li><li><p>A structured and independent working approach, combined with the ability to collaborate across technical teams.</p></li><li><p>Strong communication skills and the confidence to coordinate with internal and external stakeholders.</p></li><li><p>Good English communication skills, German is a plus.</p></li></ul><h2>WE OFFER:</h2><ul><li><p>A highly motivated, international team — we stand for openness and diversity</p></li><li><p>Independent work, flat hierarchies, and the opportunity to contribute your own ideas</p></li><li><p>Free German language courses at a centrally located partner school</p></li><li><p>Attractive discounts for Urban Sports Club memberships</p></li><li><p>Team events such as BBQs and summer parties</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/dark-matter-ggmbh/technical-project-manager-berlin-152252","tags":["Project Management"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793952061},{"slug":"product-design-engineer-berlin-303738","company_name":"Agent F GmbH","title":"Product Design Engineer","description":"<h3><strong>About Agent F</strong></h3><p>Agent F is building an autonomous finance function: software that takes on the work of keeping a company’s finances in order. That means bringing information together from different systems, recording transactions correctly, preparing useful reports, and helping people understand what needs their attention.</p><p>Today, much of this work depends on spreadsheets, repeated data entry and people checking one system against another. Our ambition is to make that work increasingly automatic, while keeping every number explainable and every consequential action under clear control.</p><p>We are building towards a complete business management system for growing companies. These founding roles will shape both the product and the way we build it.</p><h3><strong>About the role</strong></h3><p>You will own how customers experience Agent F, from landing pages and product demonstrations through onboarding and migration to the work they do every day. A founder looking at their finances for the first time and a controller investigating a discrepancy need different levels of detail. Both should understand where they are, what a number means and what to do next.</p><p>This combines product design with hands-on front-end engineering. You will talk to customers, shape the journey, design the interactions and ship them in the product. You will use AI coding agents to help implement changes, and take responsibility for reviewing the code and checking the finished experience.</p><p>Your work will connect the product into a coherent whole: consistent navigation, familiar controls and clear explanations across features. You will also own the steps that turn an interested visitor into an active, paying customer.</p><h3><strong>What you will build and improve</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>An engaging path from first interest to a useful result.</strong> Connect landing pages and product demonstrations to sign-up, account setup and the first session so a customer understands what to provide and what they will get back. Measure where people abandon the process and address the causes.</p></li><li><p><strong>A migration experience people can follow.</strong> Help customers bring in their history from accounting software or spreadsheets. Make upload progress, missing information, validation errors and next steps understandable.</p></li><li><p><strong>A consistent product experience.</strong> Develop the design language, navigation and reusable components used across the product. Make tables, forms and reports behave predictably, including loading, empty and error states.</p></li><li><p><strong>Useful decision screens.</strong> Design views that help customers compare recommendations, understand costs and choose what happens next. Our planned evidence board brings this information together as customers describe their needs.</p></li><li><p><strong>Interfaces that earn trust.</strong> Help users see where a figure came from, understand a proposed change and review it before approval. Include accessibility, keyboard use and clear language in the implementation.</p></li><li><p><strong>Improvements grounded in actual use.</strong> Keep up with the customer pipeline, from interested prospects to customers onboarding or migrating. Observe customer sessions and work with the customer-facing team. Turn recurring questions into product changes, then check whether those changes helped.</p></li></ul><p>For example, a customer uploads a file and sees a different total from the one they expected. You would design the journey that explains what was imported, what needs checking and how to resolve the difference, working with the data engineer on the underlying evidence.</p><h3><strong>What you bring</strong></h3><p>You have five or more years of experience designing and shipping software, including business-to-business software sold as a service (B2B SaaS). You may come from product design with strong engineering skills, or from front-end engineering with substantial design ownership.</p><p>You can show a product journey you improved, explain the choices you made and describe the effect on customers. You have owned an onboarding, activation or conversion measure: whether people got started, reached a useful result or became paying customers.</p><h3><strong>Core experience</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Product design across information architecture, interaction design and visual design.</p></li><li><p>Production front-end work with React, TypeScript, CSS and reusable components, including reviewing and debugging code generated by agents.</p></li><li><p>Building or maintaining a design system that other people use.</p></li><li><p>Customer research, usability testing and product analytics that inform what you ship.</p></li><li><p>Daily use of AI coding agents, with a clear approach to specifications, review and verification.</p></li><li><p>Clear written explanations of design decisions and their trade-offs.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Useful additional experience</strong></h3><p>Financial software, complex tables and dashboards, or products where people need to inspect the source of a result. Experience with configuration-driven interfaces, where shared rules and data determine how a screen is assembled, would also be useful.</p><h3><strong>What early progress could look like</strong></h3><p>In your first months, you would map the main customer journeys, establish a baseline for onboarding and conversion, and ship an improvement to a step where customers regularly get stuck. Alongside that, you would start consolidating repeated interface patterns into reusable components.</p><p>We would look for evidence that customers reach a useful result sooner, complete more of the journey independently and need less help with the interface. The exact priorities will follow the customer needs you find with the team.</p><h3><strong>Operational excellence and customer commitments</strong></h3><p>You take pride in a product customers can depend on under pressure. When sign-up, migration or a critical financial workflow breaks, you step in, establish what the customer needs and work with the team to restore a safe path forward. A misleading balance, missing transaction or incorrect status can be a financial emergency even when the page loads normally. You make the problem visible, help contain its impact and verify the complete customer journey after a fix.</p><p>Customer commitments shape how we work. You are willing to interrupt planned work, respond promptly and stay engaged when an urgent issue puts a service-level agreement (SLA), onboarding commitment or financial deadline at risk. That requires flexibility beyond normal working hours as part of agreed on-call coverage and coordinated incident response. You keep people informed and see the issue through to a verified recovery or an explicit handover. Afterwards, you improve the system so the same emergency becomes less likely.</p><h3><strong>How you will work</strong></h3><p>This is a senior founding role in a small team, with scope to shape product decisions and engineering practice. You will work closely with the engineers responsible for platform operations and customer data. You will carry work from customer observation through implementation and release, then follow up on how it performs.</p><p>Everyone shares responsibility for the whole product and the customer outcome. You will pick up the most important work or whatever is on fire, including tasks outside your specialty. You take initiative, bring in the right expertise and stay involved until the problem is resolved. Customer impact and urgency determine where you focus.</p><p>The role is full-time and in-person in Berlin. German is not required.</p><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/agent-f-gmbh/product-design-engineer-berlin-303738","tags":["Product Design","Industrial Design"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793952061},{"slug":"devops-engineer-hamburg-390544","company_name":"Clariness","title":"DevOps Engineer (f/m/d)","description":"<p><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(230, 126, 35);"><strong>Clariness is looking for a DevOps Engineer (f/m/d) based in Berlin, Hamburg, Cape Town, UK, or Serbia.<br></strong><strong>- Full-time; unlimited -</strong></span></p>
<p><span style="color: rgb(230, 126, 35); font-size: 12pt;"><strong><span data-contrast="none">About the role:</span></strong></span></p>
<p>This role is about ensuring that Clariness' global cloud infrastructure remains reliable, secure and ready to scale. You will join a collaborative technical environment where infrastructure enables our product, data engineering and AI teams to deliver meaningful solutions.</p>
<p><strong><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(230, 126, 35);">As a DevOps Engineer, you would be responsible for:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Building, operating and improving Clariness' global AWS infrastructure, with a particular focus on ECS, RDS and supporting services.</li>
<li>Managing infrastructure through Terraform, contributing to reusable, maintainable and version-controlled infrastructure as code.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Improving CI/CD pipelines and container deployment processes to support reliable, secure and efficient software delivery.</li>
<li>Supporting our production systems by monitoring infrastructure, troubleshooting incidents and contributing to improvements in reliability, security and cloud cost efficiency.</li>
<li>Collaborating with cross-functional product teams, as well as our data engineering and AI teams, to understand their requirements and provide effective infrastructure solutions.</li>
<li>Contributing to infrastructure improvement initiatives, maintaining operational documentation and supporting technical excellence across Clariness.</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="color: rgb(230, 126, 35); font-size: 12pt;"><strong>We would like you to have:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>
<ul>
<li>A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.</li>
<li>Hands-on experience working with production infrastructure on AWS, ideally including ECS, RDS and supporting services.</li>
<li>Practical experience with Terraform, including modules, state management and infrastructure changes through version control and code review.</li>
<li>Experience with CI/CD pipelines, containerized applications and production deployments.</li>
<li>Familiarity with backup and disaster recovery, high-availability configurations and safe database migrations.</li>
<li>The ability to independently deliver well-defined infrastructure tasks, explain technical trade-offs and contribute to architectural discussions.</li>
<li>Strong collaboration and communication skills (English at C1 level), along with an interest in using AI-assisted tools responsibly to support infrastructure development, testing and troubleshooting.</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(230, 126, 35);"><strong>You may ask now, why should I work for you? Let us give you a few reasons – <span data-teams="true">and you'll learn more during the process.</span></strong></span></p>
<ul>
<li>A varied and exciting job with a lot of personal responsibility in an international company, where you can develop and expand your skills.</li>
<li>Professional and personal development opportunities - incl. personal development budget.</li>
<li>Flexible working hours and mobile working.</li>
<li>Regular team events and open feedback culture.</li>
<li>A versatile field of activity and challenging projects.</li>
<li>A supportive and open company culture, providing the opportunity to collaborate with a diverse and professional team.</li>
<li>Impact healthcare by accelerating medical innovation through improved access to clinical trials, potentially bringing needed treatments to patients faster.</li>
</ul>
