sponsibility will be to improve how users discover and engage with rewards, how publishers integrate and monetize, and how value is measured and distributed across users, publishers, advertisers and Almedia.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />This is a high-ownership role for someone who can turn an ambitious product thesis into a clear strategy, a rigorous experimentation programme and a scalable platform.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you'll own</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Consumer product and engagement. </strong>Own the full user journey, from discovery and activation through onboarding, progression, and repeat reward engagement, by designing clear, motivating, product-native reward experiences and turning user behavior into measurable value for publishers and the platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Publisher platform. </strong>Shape the Link SDK and its integration experience for mobile publishers, improving developer experience, implementation quality, configurability and observability, while working with engineering on identity, events, attribution, reward delivery and fraud prevention to give publishers flexible tools without fragmenting the product into bespoke integrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Monetization and marketplace economics. </strong>Develop new rewarded monetization products for publishers, defining how rewards, publisher value and Almedia's economics fit together, by partnering with data science on pricing, segmentation, ranking and optimization to balance user experience, advertiser performance, publisher revenue and contribution margin.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experimentation and measurement. </strong>Own a rigorous experimentation portfolio across consumer experiences, integrations and monetization, using holdouts and causal measurement to isolate incremental value from correlation, by defining clear primary metrics, guardrails and maturity windows, and making explicit decisions to scale, change or stop each initiative.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Publisher and commercial leadership. </strong>Work directly with major mobile publishers, clearly explaining product capabilities, economics and measurement, by leading lighthouse launches, turning publisher feedback into scalable product decisions, and building reporting that publishers can understand and trust.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you'll bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior product experience in mobile adtech, publisher monetization, rewarded advertising, mobile gaming monetization or a closely related marketplace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience owning a consumer product involving rewards, onboarding, retention, progression or monetization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience shipping an SDK, API, developer platform or technically complex partner integration.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct ownership of revenue, pricing, yield, gross margin, advertiser performance or another meaningful economic outcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of marketplace economics and how incentives affect users, publishers and advertisers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep practical experience with experimentation, holdouts, selection bias and causal measurement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working with data science on ranking, pricing or optimization systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working directly with enterprise customers or publishers.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>What puts you ahead</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You've been a founder.</strong> You know what it means to own an outcome with no one to hand it off to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You've scaled through hyper-growth.</strong> 50 to 200+ people, building the plane mid-flight: familiar territory.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mobile gaming or advertising</strong> background. You know the players, the incentives, the dynamics.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>Why Almedia? </strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale With Almedia:</strong> Grow alongside a startup that has been profitable from day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Central Berlin Office:</strong> Work from a fully-stocked modern office built for collaboration, accessible from all around Berlin.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Other Benefits:</strong> Transport subsidy, breakfasts and lunches, language learning, Urban Sports Club, and more.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in fostering talent, evaluating all skill levels during the hiring process, and providing a clear path for growth. Almedia is an equal opportunity employer. We embrace and celebrate diversity, and encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply.</p><hr><p>Compensation: €120K – €160K</p><ul><li> • €120K – €160K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/almedia/product-lead-adtech-berlin-141161","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793947213},{"slug":"gtm-engineering-intern-revenue-operations-munich-201568","company_name":"Luminovo GmbH","title":"GTM Engineering Intern | Revenue Operations (d/f/m)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">In a nutshell: 4 to 6-month internship in our RevOps team at our Munich headquarters (hybrid), starting between February and April 2027, with the opportunity to move into a full-time role straight afterwards.</p><h3></h3><h2>About this role at Luminovo</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Luminovo builds the B2B SaaS platform that powers the electronics supply chain. DACH is our home market and one of our strongest, and we have recently expanded into North America and the rest of Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">GTM engineering at Luminovo is part of Revenue Operations, the department that sits between marketing, sales and customer success and makes sure our revenue organisation runs smoothly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our go-to-market engineering function builds the systems that find the right companies and the right people for our sales team: target lists, data enrichment, hyper-personalised outbound campaigns that signal our sellers whom to call next. We work closely with Account Executives, the BDR team and marketing and directly contribute to pipeline generation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our GTM engineering intern, you will run outbound campaigns end to end and help build the next layer: signal-based lead generation. You will also help us improve account scoring and build AI automations that take manual work off our sales reps.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There is no textbook for this role. You will learn it the way we did: by building, shipping and seeing what works.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By the end of your internship, you will have shipped revenue systems that our sales &amp; marketing teams rely on every day, and gained hands-on experience in go-to-market engineering, one of the hottest roles on the market right now!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will also see first-hand how a modern B2B start-up operates day to day, with AI built into its workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>This role is for you</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine technical thinking with commercial curiosity: perhaps you studied engineering and want to understand how companies sell, or you have discovered a passion for the commercial side of start-ups.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are keen to work in a fast-paced environment and to grow alongside a high-growth start-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring the drive to learn quickly, a sharp analytical mind and the ambition to take on real responsibility from your first weeks. You collaborate well, ask questions without hesitation and are happy to get your hands dirty.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use AI as more than a better search engine. You have built your own automations, workflows or tools, and can explain what you shipped and what came of it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are fluent in both German and English. Much of our outbound targets buyers in the DACH region, while the company operates in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You stand out if you have built something entrepreneurial during your studies, be it a side project, a student society or a small business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have first experience in GTM engineering, sales operations or automation (this is a big advantage but <u>not a requirement</u>!)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your performance objectives</h2><h3>🧬 Run outbound campaigns</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deliver multichannel campaigns end to end.</strong> Build target lists, source and enrich the right contacts, and write the messaging in German and English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go where coverage is thin.</strong> Your campaigns will go wherever our sellers need the most support or wherever there is an opportunity worth pursuing, starting with DACH and extending to the rest of Europe and North America. Take on event campaigns, new regions and opportunistic plays, and turn them around to contribute to our pipeline.</p></li></ul><h3>🌀 Build signals and tooling</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ship signals.</strong> Build plugins or scrapers that generate high-intent leads for our sellers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process scaling.</strong> Transform website engagement into automated outbound triggers and create repeatable playbooks.</p></li></ul><h3>⚙️ Build automations</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remove manual work.</strong> Automate the repetitive manual tasks our revenue teams deal with day to day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Challenge what exists.</strong> Get to know the systems we have built, then tell us where they fall short and help improve them.</p></li></ul><h3>💶 Unblock the sales team</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Understand what sales reps need.</strong> Work closely with our AEs and BDRs, get to know their accounts and processes, and remove the friction that slows them down.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Close the loop.</strong> Feed what you learn from replies and campaign results back to sales and marketing.</p></li></ul><h3>🗂 Own the data</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own enrichment and imports.</strong> Take responsibility for account enrichment and every data import into HubSpot on contact, company and lead level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep data accuracy high.</strong> You will be responsible for maintaining our enrichment so that data stays clean and workflows keep firing.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your Toolkit</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will learn to work with the most modern sales automation tools on the market, such as Clay, n8n, Twain, Lusha, Apollo, LinkedIn Sales Navigator and many more.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Work location</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our <strong>Munich</strong> headquarters. For your first two months you will be in the office most days, so you get to know the product, the team, our ICP and the basics of our market. After that, the role is <strong>hybrid</strong>, with the flexibility to work from home. Occasional travel for team retreats and industry events (expenses covered).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Whom you will be working with</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/maxhungenbach/"><strong>Max Hungenbach</strong></a>, Revenue Operations Team Lead and your line manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/danny-bodnar/"><strong>Danny Bodnar</strong></a>, GTM Engineer, your mentor and day-to-day coach</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/cliftonlobo/"><strong>Clifton Lobo</strong></a>, VP Global Sales. You will work directly with him on GTM strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dasha-vyazemskaya/"><strong>Dasha Vyazemskaya</strong></a>, Head of BDR and your partner on handing campaigns over to the BDR team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/george-k-16704a95/"><strong>George Knight</strong></a>, Demand Generation Manager in Marketing and your partner on campaigns run alongside marketing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Account Executives and BDRs</strong> across Europe and North America, for whom your campaigns run</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Skills, knowledge, and expertise</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Just so you know, we purposefully did not create a standard list of minimum qualifications for this role. We care much more about your motivation and ability to help us accelerate technical progress than we care about your CV.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re interested to find out more about why we banned requirements from our performance profiles, see <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://medium.com/startup-grind/why-we-banned-requirements-from-our-job-descriptions-33a774e1a1c2">here</a>.</p><h3></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1></h1><h1><strong>⚡️ About Luminovo</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Luminovo is the first electronics supply chain platform that unites all data, processes, and stakeholders in the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://luminovo.com/resources/blog/a-short-primer-on-the-electronics-industry?utm_campaign=employer_branding&amp;utm_source=candidate-traffic">trillion-dollar electronics industry</a>.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We fundamentally believe that technology is the best tool that humankind has developed to tackle the biggest challenges we face as a society today. And we want to do our share in accelerating technological progress. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>We bring innovations to life faster and cheaper by creating a more connected and resilient electronics supply chain.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, over 300 active customers worldwide are working with us towards this shared goal. Supported by leading investors such as Cherry Ventures, General Catalyst/LaFamiglia, Chalfen Ventures, and others, we have <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://luminovo.com/resources/blog/luminovo-raises-eu11-million-in-seed-funding-to-fix-the-broken-electronics-value-chain-with-transformative-software-suite">raised more than €20 million</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our core principles: putting people first &amp; building great things</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a remote-first company headquartered in Munich, our brilliant team is spread across cities including Munich, New York, Austin, Calgary, Berlin, London, Valencia, Nairobi, and Verona, among others. 🌍</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our team includes a mix of product enthusiasts, people advocates, business masterminds, and engineering experts. Among us are graduates from institutions like Stanford University and the University of Cambridge, as well as talented individuals with unconventional CVs. What matters most is their drive to build great things.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We provide an authentic environment based on psychological safety to empower Luminerds from various backgrounds to succeed, grow, and focus on impact. Putting people first means that we deeply care about who our employees are, what makes them unique, and what they excel at. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">See what employees and candidates have to say about Luminovo on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.kununu.com/de/luminovo">kununu</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.de/Bewertungen/luminovo-ai-Bewertungen-E2039308.htm">Glassdoor</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><hr><p>Compensation: €2,650 – €3,150 per month</p><ul><li>Intern Salary • Base Salary €2,650 – €3,150 per month</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/luminovo-gmbh/gtm-engineering-intern-revenue-operations-munich-201568","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"🇩🇪 Munich (hybrid)","created_at":1793947212},{"slug":"remote-software-engineer-operations-research-57308","company_name":"Circuithub","title":"Software Engineer, Operations Research","description":"<h2>About CircuitHub</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">CircuitHub is reshaping electronics manufacturing with The Grid, a factory-scale robotics platform that makes small-batch, high-mix electronics assembly radically more efficient. Think semiconductor-fab precision applied to the chaotic world of prototyping and low-volume production: a 10x throughput improvement in one of the world's most foundational industries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've raised $45M from top-tier investors including Plural, Y Combinator and Google Ventures, and we're already profitable. Our customers include a major EV maker, a top AI lab and many of the worlds largest companies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Grid isn't a prototype. It's live, scaling fast and delivering real revenue, and we're building the team that will scale it further.</p><h2>What you'll do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">CircuitHub builds circuit boards on demand, every order different. Each day thousands of decisions are made: which orders run on which machines, which parts to buy and when, what to promise a customer and what to charge. You'll build the models behind those decisions.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Plan the factory.</strong> Schedule orders, panels and machines across our factories for throughput and on-time delivery, and know days ahead when we will run out of work or capacity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Model the Grid.</strong> The Grid is our factory-scale robot: dozens of movers, gantries, printers and ovens. Model how work flows through it, find the bottlenecks, and tell us what the next machine or change is worth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Price and promise.</strong> Estimate what an order really costs in labour, machine time and parts, and help set prices and lead times that win work and make money.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Buy smarter.</strong> Decide what parts and consumables to stock, when to order them, and how much risk of a shortage to accept.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Put it into production.</strong> Your models don't live in a spreadsheet: they run every day, feed the planning and quoting systems, and get checked against what actually happened.</p></li></ul><h2>What we look for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A quantitative background in operations research, applied maths, statistics, quantitative finance, economics or a similar field, and a record of models that changed real decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optimisation: linear and integer programming, constraint programming, or heuristics, and judgement about when a simple rule beats a solver.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Simulation and forecasting: building a model of a messy system, calibrating it to data and saying how far to trust it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Python and SQL. You write code other people can run and rely on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use coding agents to move faster and take full ownership of what they produce.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about how things are physically made. You'll spend time in our factories in the US and UK.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manufacturing experience is welcome but not required. If you have priced risk, optimised a portfolio or forecast demand, the problems here will feel familiar.</p><h2>Stack</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Modelling:</strong> Python, OR-Tools, simulation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data:</strong> PostgreSQL, Snowflake, dbt, Dagster</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Agents:</strong> Claude Code and Codex throughout</p></li></ul><h2>Location</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote anywhere, or from our offices in London or Cambridge (UK) if you prefer, with regular visits to our factories in the UK and US.</p><h2>Pay</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">UK £80k–£125k · US $125k–$250k, depending on experience, plus equity.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £80K – £125K • Offers Equity • Multiple Ranges</p><ul><li>UK • £80K – £125K • Offers Equity</li><li>US • $125K – $250K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/circuithub/remote-software-engineer-operations-research-57308","tags":["Software Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1793947211},{"slug":"creative-strategist-producer-berlin-466898","company_name":"praxipal","title":"Creative Strategist & Producer (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TL;DR</strong> - We’re building the healthcare workforce for tomorrow. Our AI receptionist Luna is already automating patient communication in medical practices today. As the market leader in German and Austrian dentistry, and with major funding under our belt, we’re now taking the next big step: new medical specialties, new countries, new products. As Creative Strategist &amp; Producer, you own the ads that introduce medical practices to Luna, from idea to final cut, and build the in-house creative engine that keeps leads coming in every week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why praxipal?</strong> The shortage of skilled professionals is the biggest challenge in our healthcare systems. Tens of thousands of positions remain unfilled each year, and demographic shifts are only making things worse. Medical practices rely on our AI receptionist Luna to reduce staff workload and keep care accessible for everyone. We’re growing at record speed and closed a $6.7M seed round with HV Capital.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a tech-driven company that deliberately relies on a small, talent-dense team. What defines us is the speed and intensity with which we work, but just as important to us is our team spirit. That’s why we come into the office every day: to connect, learn from one another, and grow together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience producing content for paid social, ideally performance ads for Meta, at a startup, an agency or as a freelancer</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hooks, angles and conversions matter more to you than likes, and you know why an ad works or doesn’t</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A feel for what makes organic content work on Instagram and LinkedIn, and how it differs from ads</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">End-to-end skills: script, shoot, edit and design, including confident handling of cameras, lighting and audio so every shot looks and sounds professional</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A results-driven mindset: you measure your work by its impact, and you consistently deliver high-quality content at</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A portfolio that shows what you can do, ideally with numbers to back it up</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on mentality: no task is too unglamorous for you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent German and English, both written and spoken</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In short: You’ll develop and produce the ads that drive praxipal’s growth, plus the organic content that builds our brand, and build our in-house creative production from the ground up along the way.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You shape our creative strategy: you dig into our target groups, competitors and ad performance and turn your insights into ideas, hooks and angles that stop practice owners mid-scroll and get them to reach out</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write scripts for video ads, from UGC-style to testimonials to product demos</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You plan and run shoots: with customers in their practices, with our team and with creators</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You edit videos and design static ads yourself, fast and at high volume</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You deliver fresh creatives and variations every week so our campaigns never run out of steam</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You systematically test hypotheses together with our performance marketing team, analyze what works and turn the learnings into the next round of creatives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You keep a close eye on the latest content marketing trends, formats and platform features and bring fresh ideas into our creatives before everyone else does</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You also produce organic content for Instagram, LinkedIn and other channels, often by repurposing material from your ad shoots</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Get</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive base salary plus participation in our VSOP program</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real impact: your creatives directly determine how many practices we win each week, and you see the results in real time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creative freedom: you help build our creative production from scratch and grow into more responsibility at an exceptional pace</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional gear: if you don’t have your own, we provide high-quality equipment for shooting, lighting and audio</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unparalleled learning opportunities at the frontier of AI and healthcare</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work alongside a strong, motivated team with ample growth opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Urban Sports Club membership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch subsidy via Lunchit and daily team dinners covered by the company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular team events and offsites with the wider praxipal team</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/praxipal/creative-strategist-producer-berlin-466898","tags":["Go-to-Market"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793947210},{"slug":"people-ops-intern-berlin-320239","company_name":"Taktile","title":"People Ops Intern","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taktile empowers financial institutions to transform into truly AI-native organizations. We're growing rapidly with enterprise customers across banks and insurance companies, and we're looking for an <strong>HR Intern</strong> to be Taktile's ambassador to our future employees.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will collaborate closely with our People team to ensure the efficient management of the employee lifecycle, from onboarding to ongoing feedback and support. You will play a crucial role in maintaining our HR systems, keeping employee data accurate, and supporting the administrative tasks that keep our people operations running smoothly. By handling these essential tasks, you will contribute significantly to shaping the company's growth and ensuring we maintain a high standard of employee satisfaction and performance. You will work closely with colleagues across all departments to manage various HR activities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Do as an HR Intern</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employee Onboarding:</strong> Once candidates join our team, take the lead in preparing