> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/flow-engineering/senior-staff-software-engineer-product-london-26262","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793958016},{"slug":"lead-product-manager-london-466732","company_name":"Faculty","title":"Lead Product Manager","description":"<h2><strong>Why Faculty? </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We established Faculty in 2014 because we thought that AI would be the most important technology of our time. Since then, we’ve worked with over 350 global customers to transform their performance through human-centric AI. You can read about our real-world impact <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://faculty.ai/impact">here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We don’t chase hype cycles. We innovate, build and deploy responsible AI which moves the needle - and we know a thing or two about doing it well. We bring an unparalleled depth of technical, product and delivery expertise to our clients who span government, finance, retail, energy, life sciences and defence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our business, and reputation, is growing fast and we’re always on the lookout for individuals who share our intellectual curiosity and desire to build a positive legacy through technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is an epoch-defining technology, join a company where you’ll be empowered to envision its most powerful applications, and to make them happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In Faculty’s Applied AI group, we partner with ambitious organisations across private and public sectors to help them reinvent how they work, compete and serve people with AI. We bring them our extensive expertise in using AI in real-world situations and a track record of delivering serious impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product managers in Applied AI provide strategic leadership for Faculty’s clients, guiding stakeholders through discovery, decision-making and execution. We help our clients to achieve the greatest impact for their organisations with the very latest AI advancements and we teach bleeding-edge product development practices.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Lead Product Manager at Faculty, you’ll take on large strategic client engagements, leading teams that include top-flight Data Scientists, Machine Learning Engineers and Product Designers, among others. You’ll help to drive the strategic direction of high-impact AI products for our clients, balancing complex technical considerations and user needs to achieve real commercial outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building and shipping impactful products that realise the potential of frontier AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as a trusted advisor to senior stakeholders at big-name clients on their product and AI strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading discovery to identify the right problems to solve, using clear hypotheses and success measures to decide what gets built.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping teams focused on outcomes, not just outputs by defining clear goals, shaping prioritisation and articulating trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embedding innovation culture among our clients, guiding and inspiring them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborating with your cross-functional teammates including Data Scientists, Engineers, Product Designers and Delivery to set the quality bar for AI products, including the eval strategy to ensure they continue to work as intended.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building lasting product development capability in client organisations, from the habits of individual teams to the product operating model as a whole.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advising clients on how AI can accelerate and improve their product development lifecycle, from research and discovery through to delivery and measurement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributing to Faculty's product practice through developing case studies, thought leadership and repeatable methods that scale across clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partnering with Delivery leads on planning and execution, including supporting business development and fostering strong client relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coaching and developing other product managers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we're looking for:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have substantial experience conceiving, building and launching products at scale, including at least 2 years in a product leadership role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve routinely worked directly with C-suite or equivalent senior leaders at significant, successful organisations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional commercial acumen: you've made the case for new products or services - whether for revenue, savings or public benefit - and defended it with senior budget holders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You relish unstructured problems and can turn them into clear plans that teams can execute.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can comfortably converse with experts in how AI models are created, evaluated and operationalised.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have demonstrable experience in rolling out cutting-edge AI-accelerated product development processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a clear track record of mentoring team members and fostering a collaborative, ambitious culture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You show forward-thinking initiative to spot new client opportunities, solve ambiguous problems, and build enduring organisational value.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable experience</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have meaningful professional services or consulting experience, ideally with large enterprises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve held a product leadership position in at least one scaled-up, fast-moving product-led organisation, owning significant scope and achieving meaningful impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're an active voice in the product community, speaking at conferences or contributing to panels and publications.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Recruitment Ethos</strong></h2><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aim to grow the best team - not the most similar one. We know that diversity of individuals fosters diversity of thought, and that strengthens our principle of seeking truth. And we know from experience that diverse teams deliver better work, relevant to the world in which we live. We’re united by a deep intellectual curiosity and desire to use our abilities for measurable positive impact. We strongly encourage applications from people of all backgrounds, ethnicities, genders, religions and sexual orientations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don’t feel you meet all the requirements, but are excited by the role and know you bring some key strengths, please don't hesitate in applying as you might be right for this role, or other roles. We are open to conversations about part-time hours. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A note on AI: we're happy for you to use it for research and interview prep, but please don't use it to generate answers during live interviews. We also use an AI note-taker (Metaview) in interviews so interviewers can stay present (which you can opt out of just let us know,) and every application is reviewed by a human, never decided by AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/faculty/lead-product-manager-london-466732","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793958016},{"slug":"customer-director-life-sciences-london-345630","company_name":"Faculty","title":"Customer Director - Life Sciences","description":"<h2><strong>Why Faculty? </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We established Faculty in 2014 because we thought that AI would be the most important technology of our time. Since then, we’ve worked with over 350 global customers to transform their performance through human-centric AI. You can read about our real-world impact <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://faculty.ai/impact">here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We don’t chase hype cycles. We innovate, build and deploy responsible AI which moves the needle - and we know a thing or two about doing it well. We bring an unparalleled depth of technical, product and delivery expertise to our clients who span government, finance, retail, energy, life sciences and defence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our business, and reputation, is growing fast and we’re always on the lookout for individuals who share our intellectual curiosity and desire to build a positive legacy through technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is an epoch-defining technology, join a company where you’ll be empowered to envision its most powerful applications, and to make them happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bringing medicine to patients is complex, expensive and high-risk. Faculty’s Life Science’s team is concentrated on building AI solutions which optimise the research and commercialisation of life-changing therapies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We partner with major pharma firms, academic research centres and MedTech start-ups to design and deliver solutions which address critical healthcare challenges, and help to democratize health for all.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Customer Director, you’ll play an influential role in growing our most impactful accounts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will act as a strategic partner to our Life Sciences clients, helping them supercharge their operations and end-user engagement through AI-powered decision-making. Leading a high-performing team of delivery and engagement specialists, you’ll oversee complex commercial negotiations, ensure the successful delivery of cutting-edge Applied AI solutions, and build key relationships which position Faculty as the global leader in AI-driven transformation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-PRIO</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driving revenue growth;  identifying strategic opportunities to expand current accounts and onboarding new clients within your sector</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Developing and implementing robust strategic account plans that align Faculty’s AI solutions with client business objectives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading commercial negotiations and partnering with the Business Unit Director on accurate sales planning and forecasting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building trusted relationships with senior budget holders and C-suite stakeholders to ensure high levels of client satisfaction and retention</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Managing and mentoring cross-functional commercial teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Representing Faculty at industry events and networking forums to build a reputation as a thought leader in AI-driven transformation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborating with technical teams to translate complex data concepts into innovative use cases that solve real-world client problems</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve managed senior, complex stakeholder relationships in the Life Sciences industry - some experience in consulting preferred</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience leading large-scale AI/digital transformation projects</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You possess a strong business development mindset with experience in sales methodologies and the end-to-end management of deal processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a practical problem solver with the forensic skills to scope a problem, identify client needs and implement effective solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a compelling communicator - comfortable collaborating with technical experts and translating data-oriented concepts for non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring experience in team mentorship and coaching</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have demonstrated capability to balance multiple strategic projects simultaneously, while maintaining a focus on quality and commercial impact</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our interview process</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talent Team Screen: 40 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introduction Interview: 60 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial Interview: 60 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership and Principles interview: 60 mins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meet the MD, Commercial: 30 mins</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Recruitment Ethos</strong></h2><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aim to grow the best team - not the most similar one. We know that diversity of individuals fosters diversity of thought, and that strengthens our principle of seeking truth. And we know from experience that diverse teams deliver better work, relevant to the world in which we live. We’re united by a deep intellectual curiosity and desire to use our abilities for measurable positive impact. We strongly encourage applications from people of all backgrounds, ethnicities, genders, religions and sexual orientations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you don’t feel you meet all the requirements, but are excited by the role and know you bring some key strengths, please don't hesitate in applying as you might be right for this role, or other roles. We are open to conversations about part-time hours. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A note on AI: we're happy for you to use it for research and interview prep, but please don't use it to generate answers during live interviews. We also use an AI note-taker (Metaview) in interviews so interviewers can stay present (which you can opt out of just let us know,) and every application is reviewed by a human, never decided by AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/faculty/customer-director-life-sciences-london-345630","tags":["Business Growth"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793958016},{"slug":"people-and-workplace-executive-london-378342","company_name":"Healf","title":"People and Workplace Executive","description":"<h1><strong>Redefine wellbeing </strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healf is Europe's fastest-growing company: top of the FT1000, top of the Sifted 100. We've grown from £1m to £100m+ in under three years with a lean, talent-dense team and day-one founder intensity. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're operators, engineers, athletes, former and future founders redefining what wellbeing means for tens of millions of people.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We curate the world's best wellbeing brands across The Four Pillars™: EAT, MOVE, MIND, SLEEP. That's the first chapter.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The next chapter is harder and more interesting. We're moving from one market to many, from e-commerce to a technology platform, from curating wellbeing to defining it. We're building the world's best health team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an ambitious <strong>People Executive</strong> to help build an exceptional employee experience at Healf.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an ideal opportunity for an exceptional graduate or someone early in their career who thrives on ownership, loves bringing order to fast-moving environments, and genuinely cares about creating a workplace where people can do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll sit at the heart of the business, ensuring our office runs seamlessly, every new joiner has an outstanding experience, and our culture continues to scale as we grow. You'll constantly look for ways to improve processes, automate manual work, and raise the bar across every employee touchpoint.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Where you'll make an impact</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Workplace:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create a workplace that is organised, energising and enables the team to perform at their best.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the day-to-day running of the office, ensuring spaces, meeting rooms and equipment are always ready for use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage workplace technology, inventory and supplies, proactively identifying improvements before they become problems.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture and Engagement:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launch initiatives that strengthen team connection, including buddy programmes, coffee chats and other engagement activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate inspiring fireside chats, team meetings and internal events.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan quarterly socials and wellbeing initiatives aligned to Healf's four wellbeing pillars.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gather feedback from employees and identify opportunities to improve the overall employee experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul></li></ul><h2><strong>What you'll bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly organised with exceptional attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Naturally proactive; you spot problems before anyone else does.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong ownership mentality; you enjoy being trusted with responsibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to prioritise multiple projects in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious and always looking for better ways of working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident working across different teams and building relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong administrative skills and comfortable learning new systems quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Positive energy and genuine enthusiasm for creating a great employee experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excited by working in the office five days a week and helping shape company culture in person.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous internship or placement in People, Operations, Hospitality, Events or Customer Experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using tools such as Slack, Google Workspace, Humaans, and ai tools like Claude Code or Codex.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience organising events or running projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience improving processes or introducing automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passion for wellbeing, health or high-performance cultures.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What makes someone exceptional in this role?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We'd love to see examples of someone who has:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taken ownership of a university society, sports club or large-scale event.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Built systems that made something run better.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Naturally notices details that others miss.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Loves hosting, organising and creating memorable experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has high standards and dislikes leaving things "good enough."</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learns incredibly quickly and actively seeks feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Brings energy to a room and enjoys helping others succeed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">These behaviours matter far more than extensive experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Our interview process</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 minutes with the Talent team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 minutes with the People team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">60 minutes case study with the People team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 minutes with Lestat, Co-founder</p></li></ul><h2>The Deal</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We ask for full ownership and a genuine commitment to give this chapter everything you have. In return, we'll give you everything we have, invested in your growth, your wellbeing and the defining skills of the next decade.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've built the fastest-growing company in Europe with a team small enough that every person in it shapes the outcome. If that's for you- hit apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/healf/people-and-workplace-executive-london-378342","tags":["Performance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office","created_at":1793958016},{"slug":"head-of-india-london-449890","company_name":"Taptapsend","title":"Head of India","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">India is the biggest remittance market with over $130 billion a year flowing home to it, from everywhere: engineers in the Bay Area and Sydney, cabbies in Toronto, construction crews in Dubai, shopkeepers in Leicester, students in Berlin. From Punjabis, Gujaratis, Tamils, Malayalis and Telugus. From people wiring $3,000 a month to a Mumbai mortgage and people sending $80 to a village in Bihar. Your job is to win this market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are someone who gets excited by the nuances of the Indian diaspora and how to reach each group, and who wants to own the P&amp;L, the regulatory landscape and pricing at the same time. If you find the price sensitivity of each cohort exciting, and "why do Malayali nurses cluster in specific hospital systems, and what does that mean for acquisition?" as interesting as "what's RBI's latest remittance policy and which banks make the best partners," this is it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the GM, you own the P&amp;L, and set pricing. For customer growth, you decide which communities to acquire and in what order. Know the RBI's rules well enough to see the openings inside them, not just the limits. A Gujarati family in New Jersey and a Punjabi trucker in Brampton got abroad through completely different networks, and reaching them takes completely different channels.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reports to the Head of South Asia. Builds a team of FX Advisors in India and growth managers in sending markets. The face of India inside and outside the company. Total ownership. Be your own CEO</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Own</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The P&amp;L. Volume, gross profit and CAC across every India corridor. Not influence, own. A miss is your miss. A beat is your win.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strategy and sequencing. Which sender markets, which communities, which channels, in what order. US, Canada, UK, Europe, Australia and UAE to start. Build the plan, defend it to leadership, execute it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pricing. India is the most rate-sensitive, most competitive remittance market in the world, up against competitors who reprice daily. Set FX and fee strategy corridor by corridor.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The regulatory and partner landscape. RBI rules, bank partnerships, payout rails. Know the terrain cold and own the local relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product. Obsess over UX and the services NRIs actually need. Closer to the customer than anyone in the company, and what you hear feeds straight into product, pricing and customer support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The diaspora puzzle. Community partnerships, temples and gurdwaras and churches, cricket leagues, student associations, remittance-heavy employers, influencers, festivals (Diwali is a season, not a day). Get in front of each community authentically, and cheaply.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team. Hire, coach and retain people in India and in sending markets. Small, dense, fast.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10 to 15 years in high-growth environments: startups, operations, consulting, finance, fintech. Has owned a number and talks about it the way owners do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diaspora-fluent. Real knowledge of and networks in the Indian diaspora, and real curiosity about it. Migration patterns, community structures, who sends money to whom and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercially sharp. Holds pricing, unit economics and CAC math in their head, and works the data directly. Excel or Sheets required, SQL a real plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hustler with judgment. Closes a bank partnership Monday, reviews corridor margins Tuesday, shows up at a community event in Jackson Heights on Saturday. Likes all three.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A regulatory realist. Understands (or can quickly master) RBI rules and the compliance realities of moving money into India. Treats compliance as a partner, not an obstacle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Multilingual, ideally. Fluent in English. Hindi, Gujarati, Punjabi, Tamil, Telugu or Malayalam are genuine assets.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: London or Dubai. Regular travel to India and sending markets is part of the job.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why This Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">India is the largest remittance market in the world, and winning it moves the whole company forward. This role owns that outcome, with the authority and the accountability that come with it. It also drives real value for the customers: Immigrants work hard for this money, and every basis point saved goes home.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building the world’s leading cross-border fintech for emerging markets - empowering families, fuelling local economies, and changing how millions access financial services.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since our launch in 2019, we have transformed how money moves across borders with our operations spanning 6 out of 7 continents and covering both the busiest and most underserved  (remittance) corridors. We tapped into a massive shift - from banks to phones - bringing digital finance to places where traditional systems never reached. The next stage of growth will fuel a network of services and products especially designed to make money more accessible to diaspora communities including local cards, and additional savings and payments features.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing fast, backed by world-class investors, and scaling a product that blends <strong>real world impact with cutting edge fintech innovation</strong>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here’s a little more:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founded by Harvard grads and 3-time founders</strong> who previously built Segovia (acquired) and GiveDirectly (&gt;$300M revenue, fastest-growing NGO in the world)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Backed by top investors</strong> including Spark Capital, Canaan, Reid Hoffman, Breyer Capital, Unbound, Wamda, and more</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Built by global top performers</strong> from Bain, Google, McKinsey, Uber, Checkout, Bolt, and beyond - we move fast, stay humble, and care deeply about our mission</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Truly global team</strong> - 250+ people, 50+ nationalities, 50+ languages</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Guided by our values</strong> - ownership, impact, humility, and heart - in deed, not just word</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://www.taptapsend.com/our-values"><u>Taptap Values </u></a></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact first</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team next</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accept reality</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Propose solutions</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win with grit</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be proactively candid, with yourself and others</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Love the particular</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own it</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create positive energy</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maybe, even have fun</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taptap Send is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to building an inclusive and diverse workforce. All employment decisions are decided on the basis of qualifications, experience and business need. We strongly encourage applications who are members of underrepresented communities to apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you require reasonable adjustments to be made during the recruitment process, please do not hesitate to let us know. Any information you provide us in this respect will only be used to accommodate your requirements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Note: we recognize imposter syndrome is real - any candidate that does not perfectly fit every characteristic of this role is still strongly encouraged to apply.  </em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/taptapsend/head-of-india-london-449890","tags":["Markets"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793958015},{"slug":"product-operations-associate-london-493911","company_name":"incident.io","title":"Product Operations Associate","description":"<h1>A little about us</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a> is the AI software reliability platform trusted by engineering teams at Notion, Linear, Ramp and 2,000+ companies who can't afford downtime.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The stakes are real, the talent is insane, and somehow it's a genuinely lovely place to work. We all pull our weight, go the extra mile, and put in the bit of magic most companies don't have time for, all while having fun and never taking ourselves too seriously.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've raised $100+ million from Index Ventures, Insight Partners, and Point Nine, and we're growing fast. There's never been a better time to join.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring a Product Ops Associate to work closely with our Product Management team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is about is about giving leverage to our product leaders. You’ll pick up a mix of strategic and hands-on work — sometimes shaping big decisions, other times rolling up your sleeves to get the basics right. Both matter. You might be driving projects like pushing through legal and financial documentation to get local branches set up across the world or ensuring that GTM is getting all relevant customer feedback back to Product. The common thread: it's important, and it needs doing well.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be dropped into unfamiliar situations. You’ll need to learn quickly, and be trusted to make good calls. You’ll need to be comfortable with ambiguity, happy to work things out from first principles, and confident context switching often. The work is not always glamorous (not much of startup work is!), but it’s always meaningful.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a great fit for someone who’s curious, quick, and thrives in ambiguity. You’ll get a front-row seat to how we build and scale products — ideal if you want to continue within an operations-esque role or continue to work within some related product role. It’s also great if you want exposure to the scale-up world before choosing where to specialise.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What that looks like day to day</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as a right hand to our Product Managers: someone who can be trusted to just figure it out</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">While you will be working in Product, you’ll be expected to build relationships and get stuff done with leaders across all functions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Breaking down big, messy problems into actionable steps and delivering results</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Switching between projects (like figuring out how to extend the reach and stability of our telecom operations) and hands-on work (like supporting our Salesforce application process)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spotting inefficiencies or gaps and putting systems in place to fix them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Doing the unglamorous work when it matters because sometimes, that’s what’s needed</p></li></ul><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a fast-paced environment (e.g. startup, consulting, banking, founding experience)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High ownership and bias to action above all else, you get things done</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fast learner with strong analytical thinking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident communicator who works well across functions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with ambiguity, and quick to bring clarity</p></li></ul><h2>Supporting you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work hard and we think life outside work matters just as much. Our benefits pack is built to support both.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private medical insurance.</strong> Seriously good cover - we want you and the people you love to be looked after.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive annual leave.</strong> Showing up at your best requires switching off, and we make sure you have time to do that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Friday of every month off.</strong> Yes, seriously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced pension.</strong> We put real money in, because future-you deserves better than an afterthought.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meaningful equity.</strong> We're rapidly scaling, and everyone who helps shape the outcome should share in it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlimited AI spend.</strong> For everyone, not just engineers. We're all-in on AI across the company, and we 