ns associated with these CV's will be null and void.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/duffel/head-of-technical-support-london-446866","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, United Kingdom","created_at":1793958015},{"slug":"senior-staff-product-manager-london-307308","company_name":"V7Labs.com","title":"Senior / Staff Product Manager","description":"<h2><strong>V7</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At V7, we’re building AI platforms that help humans do their best work, at incredible scale and speed. Our mission is to turn human knowledge into trustworthy AI, making complex tasks faster, smarter, and more accurate.  We’re growing fast, backed by leading investors and AI pioneers (including the minds behind Transformers and Gemini).  <br /></p><h2></h2><h2><strong>The product</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">V7 Go helps teams turn complex, repeatable work into AI workflows they can run, review and improve<strong>.</strong> Built for private markets, insurance and real estate, it supports investment diligence, underwriting, claims review and portfolio reporting—from analysing documents and data to generating deliverables and updating connected systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your experts define how the work should be done. V7 combines reusable Skills, shared company knowledge and configurable workflows, with citations, audit logs and human review to help teams verify results and control key decisions. It supports models including GPT, Claude and Gemini.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build workflows around your processes.</strong> Configure each stage, choose models and tools, and set review steps where human judgement matters. Teams can inspect sources, correct outputs and refine workflows over time. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.v7labs.com/tables">Explore workflows</a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Give every workflow your firm’s knowledge.</strong> The <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.v7labs.com/context-graph">Context Graph</a> connects documents, entities, relationships and source evidence, creating institutional memory that teams and agents can draw on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn analysis into work your team can use.</strong> Generate editable memos, reports, presentations and spreadsheets, and connect workflows to the tools your business already uses. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.v7labs.com/slides">Explore document generation</a>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have a look at what we’re building for <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PIRJciI62Rc&amp;t=2s">finance</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PSrH97RnHIw&amp;t=5s">insurance</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The team you’ll be joining and the impact you’ll have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll own V7 Go. That’s the whole product, not a corner of it, working with engineers, designers and with the founders close by.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Go 4x-ed revenue last year with 160%+ upsell, and we’re running tens of millions of documents through it for customers in finance, insurance and real estate. What you choose to build next is what decides where that goes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The product does a lot of different things for a lot of different teams. A big part of the job is having a view on what it should be, and being willing to say no to the rest.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a small product team, so there’s not much process to hide behind. If something’s broken or missing, it’s yours to sort out.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing from day one</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning the roadmap. Deciding what gets built, killing the stuff that doesn’t matter, and shipping continuously rather than in quarterly chunks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working out which problems are actually worth solving. Sales wants one thing, the loudest customer wants another, and the interesting bet is usually neither.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Defining what good looks like before anything gets built, then checking afterwards whether it landed. Adoption, not shipped tickets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Making the trade-off calls. What’s in, what’s out, what’s deliberately a bit rubbish for now, and being able to explain why to whoever asks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Writing things down clearly. Decisions, trade-offs, why we said no to something. It’s how a small team stays pointed the same way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keeping the whole thing coherent. Workflows, Context Graph and chat need to feel like one product rather than three that happen to share a login. Most of the features are self-serve, so if it needs explaining, that's a product problem.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve owned a product properly, at a startup or somewhere with a serious product culture. Not running a backlog someone else set.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've owned a real product area end to end at a startup or a company with a serious product culture. Discovery through launch, not backlog management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built for expert users who know their domain bet