<p><span style="color: rgb(230, 126, 35); font-size: 12pt;"><strong><span data-contrast="none">About the role:</span></strong></span></p>
<p>This role is about ensuring that Clariness' global cloud infrastructure remains reliable, secure and ready to scale. You will join a collaborative technical environment where infrastructure enables our product, data engineering and AI teams to deliver meaningful solutions.</p>
<p><strong><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(230, 126, 35);">As a DevOps Engineer, you would be responsible for:</span></strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Building, operating and improving Clariness' global AWS infrastructure, with a particular focus on ECS, RDS and supporting services.</li>
<li>Managing infrastructure through Terraform, contributing to reusable, maintainable and version-controlled infrastructure as code.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Improving CI/CD pipelines and container deployment processes to support reliable, secure and efficient software delivery.</li>
<li>Supporting our production systems by monitoring infrastructure, troubleshooting incidents and contributing to improvements in reliability, security and cloud cost efficiency.</li>
<li>Collaborating with cross-functional product teams, as well as our data engineering and AI teams, to understand their requirements and provide effective infrastructure solutions.</li>
<li>Contributing to infrastructure improvement initiatives, maintaining operational documentation and supporting technical excellence across Clariness.</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="color: rgb(230, 126, 35); font-size: 12pt;"><strong>We would like you to have:&nbsp;</strong></span></p>
<ul>
<li>A degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.</li>
<li>Hands-on experience working with production infrastructure on AWS, ideally including ECS, RDS and supporting services.</li>
<li>Practical experience with Terraform, including modules, state management and infrastructure changes through version control and code review.</li>
<li>Experience with CI/CD pipelines, containerized applications and production deployments.</li>
<li>Familiarity with backup and disaster recovery, high-availability configurations and safe database migrations.</li>
<li>The ability to independently deliver well-defined infrastructure tasks, explain technical trade-offs and contribute to architectural discussions.</li>
<li>Strong collaboration and communication skills (English at C1 level), along with an interest in using AI-assisted tools responsibly to support infrastructure development, testing and troubleshooting.</li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(230, 126, 35);"><strong>You may ask now, why should I work for you? Let us give you a few reasons – <span data-teams="true">and you'll learn more during the process.</span></strong></span></p>
<ul>
<li>A varied and exciting job with a lot of personal responsibility in an international company, where you can develop and expand your skills.</li>
<li>Professional and personal development opportunities - incl. personal development budget.</li>
