de se développer grâce à une approche innovante mêlant inclusion, sensibilisation et expérience client.</p><p>Rejoindre Dans le Noir ?, c'est intégrer un groupe d'entreprises engagé qui place la diversité, l'innovation sociale et l'humain au cœur de ses projets.</p><h2>Vos missions</h2><p><strong>Basé(e) à Paris</strong>, vous participerez au développement de la visibilité digitale de <strong>notre activité au Royaume-Uni</strong>, et plus particulièrement de notre établissement <strong>londonien</strong>, l'un des plus importants du réseau.</p><p>Vous travaillerez en étroite collaboration avec les équipes françaises et britanniques afin de développer notre présence sur les réseaux sociaux et renforcer notre notoriété auprès du public anglais.</p><p>Vos principales missions :</p><ul><li><p>Participer à la définition et au déploiement de la stratégie social media pour le marché britannique.</p></li><li><p>Concevoir et produire des contenus engageants adaptés aux différentes plateformes (Instagram, TikTok, Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube).</p></li><li><p>Réaliser des photos, vidéos, Reels, Stories et autres formats créatifs.</p></li><li><p>Élaborer et suivre le calendrier éditorial.</p></li><li><p>Assurer la publication et l'animation quotidienne des réseaux sociaux.</p></li><li><p>Interagir avec les communautés et contribuer au développement de l'engagement.</p></li><li><p>Analyser les performances des contenus et des campagnes (reporting, KPIs, recommandations).</p></li><li><p>Effectuer une veille régulière sur les tendances digitales, les nouveautés des plateformes et les bonnes pratiques du secteur.</p></li><li><p>Participer ponctuellement à des déplacements à Londres pour la création de contenus et la couverture d'événements ou d'actualités locales.</p></li></ul><h2>Vos compétences</h2><ul><li><p>Étudiant(e) en communication, marketing digital, école de commerce ou formation équivalente (Bac +4 / Bac +5).</p></li><li><p>Excellente maîtrise de l'anglais à l'écrit comme à l'oral (niveau C1/C2 indispensable).</p></li><li><p>Bonne connaissance des principaux réseaux sociaux et de leurs codes.</p></li><li><p>À l'aise avec les outils de création de contenus (Canva, CapCut, Adobe Express, suite Adobe ou équivalent).</p></li><li><p>Intérêt marqué pour la création de contenus photo et vidéo.</p></li><li><p>Créatif(ve), autonome, organisé(e) et force de proposition.</p></li><li><p>Sensibilité aux tendances digitales et curiosité pour les nouveaux formats de communication.</p></li></ul><p><em>Une première expérience en gestion de réseaux sociaux ou création de contenus serait appréciée.</em></p><h2>Modalités du stage</h2><ul><li><p>Type de contrat : stage de 6 mois</p></li><li><p>Déplacements à Londres ponctuellement</p></li><li><p>Rémunération : indemnisation légale </p></li><li><p>Prise en charge à 50% de l’abonnement aux transports en commun</p></li><li><p><strong>Date de démarrage : février 2027</strong></p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/ethik-investment/stage-social-media-digital-communication-marche-britannique-h-f-paris-394447","tags":["Marketing Assistant"],"job_types":["Convention de stage","internship"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1793959352},{"slug":"gestionnaire-facturation-h-f-ivry-sur-seine-47399","company_name":"UNIK AND CO","title":"Gestionnaire facturation (h/f)","description":"<h2>À propos de UNIK AND CO</h2><p>Unik&Co est un cabinet de recrutement spécialisé dans le recrutement en CDI, CDD et Intérim sur les fonctions supports, financières et supply chain. Basé à Paris, nous pilotons les recrutements sur la France entière pour des acteurs des secteurs de l’Industrie & Santé, de la Banque & Assurance, et du Commerce, Retail et Grande Distribution.</p><h2>Vos missions au quotidien</h2><p>Vous intervenez en support opérationnel pour garantir la gestion et la fluidité des flux de facturation au sein du service dédié.</p><ul><li><p>Gérer la boîte e-mails du service et traiter les demandes entrantes.</p></li><li><p>Effectuer la saisie des avoirs fabricants dans le système de gestion.</p></li><li><p>Prendre en charge les litiges de facturation liés aux quantités ou à la qualité des produits en lien direct avec les différents services.</p></li></ul><h2>Votre rémunération et vos avantages</h2><p>La rémunération annuelle brute est fixée à EUR 29,000–30,000.</p><p>Vous bénéficiez d'une mutuelle santé ainsi que de la participation aux frais de transports publics.</p><h2>Vos premiers mois</h2><p>Dès votre arrivée en contrat temporaire de 39 heures par semaine basé à Ivry-sur-Seine avec une organisation en mode hybride, vous prenez en main la gestion des flux de facturation et le traitement des demandes et des litiges. Vous intégrez une équipe au sein d'un contrat de 4 mois comprenant 25 jours de vacances par an.</p><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/unik-and-co/gestionnaire-facturation-h-f-ivry-sur-seine-47399","tags":["Accounts Receivable"],"job_types":["Ctt - contrat de travail temporaire","interim","professionnel / expérimenté"],"location":"Ivry-sur-Seine","created_at":1793959352},{"slug":"developer-advocate-france-paris-271663","company_name":"Adapty.io","title":"Developer Advocate (France)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">More than 30,000 subscription apps run on Adapty: $5B in revenue tracked, 4B users served, 80B API calls a month. That's one of the richest datasets in the app economy. Our mission is simple: make apps rich.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a team of 210+ passionate, product-driven people who love solving big challenges. Backed by top investors like 500 Startups and Surface Ventures, we are building one of mobile's fastest-growing SaaS companies and aiming for number one worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the French Adapty developer community from close to zero.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Show up at French mobile and developer events, and speak when it makes sense.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run Adapty's own meetups, webinars and workshops in France.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create content for French developers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build relationships with local communities, organisers and companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pass interested teams you meet at events to our Sales team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to build a developer community and have the energy to do it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've run or helped run a community, spoken at events, or you understand how developer communities work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You like being around developers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're based in France and speak French and English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to know subscriptions or our product. We'll teach you.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Google Developer Expert status</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Speaking experience at meetups or conferences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your own developer content: YouTube, blog, podcast</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A mobile development background</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What's in it for you</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product with industry-best metrics. Adapty is among the top 5% fastest-growing SaaS companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional compensation directly tied to your results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct communication and ownership. No bureaucracy, no politics, just impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible remote work. Join us from anywhere or work onsite in our Belgrade or London offices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional support. Language learning, sports, health insurance, laptop coverage, and more.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/adaptyio/developer-advocate-france-paris-271663","tags":["Adapty"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1793958016},{"slug":"product-marketer-paris-2757","company_name":"Dust","title":"Product Marketer","description":"<h1><strong>About Dust</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work is being rewritten, and the people holding the pen are the ones who actually run it.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With enterprise-grade governance, flexible model choice, and a collaborative interface for humans and agents to work together, Dust empowers AI Operators at the world’s fastest-moving companies to rewire how work gets done.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With 70%+ weekly active users, people stick with Dust as much as they do with Slack and Notion. We don't get piloted and shelved. We land once, and spread. <strong>We're at an exciting stage of our journey, and growing fast.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're serving <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://dust.tt/customers">great customers</a> like Datadog, 1Password, Cursor, Clay, Vanta and Persona, and aim to x5 our growth by the end of 2026.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dust is backed by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://techcrunch.com/2024/06/27/dust-grabs-another-16-million-for-its-enterprise-ai-assistants-connected-to-internal-data/">Sequoia</a> with a determined team of optimists (coming from Stripe, OpenAI, and Stanford) who like to focus on users, ship fast, and don't take themselves too seriously while doing so. The Generalist <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/dust-tt_were-honored-to-be-recognized-on-the-generalists-activity-7359284343929741313-Rq04">named us among the Future 50</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Summary</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dust is looking for a Product Marketer to shape how we bring a fast-moving, technical product to market and build the engine behind our product launches.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will lead product launches and storytelling at Dust, turning a constant stream of product innovation into clear positioning, compelling narratives, and launches that help customers understand what’s new, why it matters, and what they can do with it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role. You will work closely with product and engineering to understand what we’re building, find the story within it, and bring that story to life across messaging, web, video, social, customer communications, and sales enablement. You’ll own the work from strategy through execution, bringing in designers, contractors, and other partners where they can add specialist expertise.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a rare opportunity to help define the product narrative of a category-defining AI company while the product, the market, and the way people work with AI are all evolving quickly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What you'll do</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Own Dust’s product launch motion</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own product launches from initial narrative and positioning through asset creation, amplification strategy, and sales enablement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and run an always-on launch program that keeps pace with Dust’s rapid product development, supporting at least 5-7 releases each quarter</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with engineering team to understand what’s shipping, why it matters, and which initiatives require a broader market moment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish lightweight launch tiers and processes that bring consistency without slowing the team down</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Turn product innovation into compelling stories</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop positioning and messaging for new capabilities, translating technical innovation into clear, differentiated narratives that resonate with Dust’s buyers and users</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create launch assets across formats, including short-form videos, social campaigns, web copy, blogs, livestream events, customer communications, and sales collateral</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop unique, scroll-stopping feature overview videos by owning storyboarding and screen capture end-to-end, while leveraging in-house creative and design support or external contractors as needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experiment with new formats and approaches to find the most effective ways to make Dust’s product understandable, memorable, and exciting</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Become a trusted partner to product and engineering</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong relationships with engineers and user leads and become a partner they proactively bring into product launches</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop enough technical fluency to ask the right questions, challenge assumptions, and uncover the most important customer and market story</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operate effectively in Dust’s highly autonomous product environment, where engineers often lead product initiatives directly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring customer, competitive, and market context into conversations about how we position and communicate the product</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Dust’s founders and marketing leadership on major product narratives and moments</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Connect product storytelling across the business</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equip Sales and Customer Success teams with the messaging, assets, and context they need to effectively pitch new capabilities to customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Brand &amp; Content to turn product innovation into broader editorial and content opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Growth and Field Marketing to extend launches across campaigns, events, and distribution channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure Dust’s product positioning and differentiation remain clear and consistent as the platform evolves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create a reliable pipeline of high-quality product content that teams across Dust can use and distribute</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you’ll bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3–5+ years of dedicated product marketing experience, ideally with strong PMM foundations from an established B2B technology company and hands-on experience in a high-growth startup</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of personally owning technical B2B product or feature launches from positioning through execution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional product storytelling skills, with the ability to make complex technology clear, credible, and compelling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The range to create across formats, including positioning and messaging, web, written content, social, presentations, and video or demo storytelling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical curiosity and the ability to build credibility with engineers by asking thoughtful questions and quickly getting fluent in the product</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong taste and an informed point of view on what great modern product marketing looks like</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort operating with ambiguity and figuring out the right approach rather than defaulting to an established playbook</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on working style. You’re as comfortable writing the copy, developing the storyboard, or building the launch plan as you are setting the strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep fluency in and curiosity about AI. You’ll use Dust to run your own function and become deeply familiar with how our customers are putting AI to work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Paris</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're prioritizing building our team with an in-person culture at our offices in Paris, London, San Francisco, and New York because we value the magic that happens when talented people work closely together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have an office-first culture. Some of the best things about building at Dust are the energy, the fast decisions, and the unexpected conversations that unlock a hard problem, which happen because we are in the same room. Being together is not a formality, it is how we do our best work, and it is something we actively protect.<br /><br />That s