location":"Paris, Île-de-France, France","created_at":1793957467},{"slug":"technology-transformation-senior-paris-393604","company_name":"EIGHT ADVISORY SAS","title":"Technology Transformation - Senior","description":"<p style="text-align:start;">Eight Advisory est un cabinet leader sur le marché du conseil financier et opérationnel, indépendant, spécialisé en Transaction, Restructuration et Transformation d’entreprises.</p><p style="text-align:start;">Nous accompagnons les dirigeants, les actionnaires, les banques et les investisseurs potentiels dans leurs décisions.</p><p style="text-align:start;">En très forte croissance depuis notre création fin 2009, Eight Advisory compte aujourd’hui plus de 1100 collaborateurs dont 129 associés et continue de se développer. Nous sommes présents en France, Belgique, Allemagne, Royaume-Uni, Suisse,&nbsp;Pays-Bas,&nbsp;USA,&nbsp;Espagne, Italie ainsi que&nbsp;dans une trentaine d’autres villes dans le monde à travers notre réseau de cabinets indépendants&nbsp;"Eight International".</p><p><br></p><p>Dans le cadre de nos missions, nous axons notre développement sur une approche mixte IT et financière, du diagnostic jusqu’à la mise en place des recommandations et nous intervenons en collaboration étroite avec les membres de la Direction Générale.<br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>En rejoignant notre équipe Transformation IT, vous interviendrez principalement dans les contextes suivants :</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong>Accompagnement des opérations M&amp;A</strong> :</p><ul><li><p>Dans un contexte de transaction, vous participerez aux « IT Due Diligences » dans lesquels vous présenterez un état des lieux de l’entreprise d’un point de vue IT : organisation de la DSI, stratégie et projets, infrastructure, applications, analyses des dépenses IT.</p></li><li><p>Dans un contexte de détourage d’actifs</p><ul><li><p>Vous réaliserez une « IT Due Diligence » de ou des entités concernées en insistant sur les enjeux de dépendance et d’adhérence vis-à-vis du groupe / du vendeur ;</p></li><li><p>Vous évaluerez les éléments IT ayant un impact sur la valeur des actifs ;</p></li><li><p>Vous participerez à l’élaboration de plan de séparation et à la rédaction des TSA.</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Dans un contexte d’intégration</p><ul><li><p>Vous définirez la stratégie d’intégration de l’entité cible, la recherche de synergies, la définition et la déclinaison opérationnelle de projets d’intégration, l’optimisation des coûts et du planning d’intégration ;</p></li><li><p>Vous challengerez les propositions d’intégration d’éventuels prestataires.</p></li><li><p>Vous participerez au suivi des différents chantiers d’intégration.</p></li></ul></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><strong>Conduite de la transformation IT &amp; Digitale :</strong></p><ul><li><p>Vous participerez à la définition de plans de transformation IT et digitale, visant à soutenir la stratégie de développement ou de reconstruction de l’entreprise ;</p></li><li><p>Vous travaillerez à l’élaboration de schémas directeurs : planning, coûts, ressources, priorisation des projets, etc. ;</p></li><li><p>Vous pourrez suivre et piloter les différents chantiers de ce schéma directeur pour en assurer le bon déroulement.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><p><strong>Pilotage et amélioration de la performance </strong>:</p><ul><li><p>Vous assisterez nos clients dans l’amélioration et le contrôle de leur performance IT, en particulier à l’audit de projets IT et à la revue de la performance de la DSI ;</p></li><li><p>Vous accompagnerez nos clients dans la rédaction de cahier des charges, en les assistant dans le choix des outils répondant à leurs besoins ;</p></li><li><p>Vous participerez à la définition et mise en œuvre de plan d’actions impactant l’EBITDA et/ou la trésorerie (réduction des coûts IT, réorganisation de la DSI, optimisation des projets, etc.) ;</p></li><li><p>Dans le cadre d’un accompagnement de nos clients en situation de perte de rentabilité, manque de visibilité ou de compréhension des flux de la part des managers (actionnaires ou société mère), vous participerez à la réalisation de diagnostics mêlant finance &amp; IT, à l’accompagnement à la renégociation de contrats, à l’élaboration de plans d’amélioration de la rentabilité et de rationalisation de la DSI, puis à la mise en œuvre opérationnelle.</p></li></ul></li></ul> <br> <p>Nous recherchons pour ces missions des candidats de formation supérieure (Bac+5 –école d’ingénieur ou école de commerce de rang A), ayant acquis une&nbsp;expérience probante parmi les suivantes :</p><ul><li><p>Une expérience dans le conseil durant laquelle il/elle aura développé de solides compétences IT &amp; digitales avec une appétence pour l’analyse des impacts financiers attendus.</p></li><li><p>Une expérience opérationnelle dans une structure reconnue pour son excellence dans les domaines informatiques et / ou digitaux.</p></li><li><p>Une bonne connaissances des outils présents sur le marché.</p></li></ul><p>Vous êtes dotés de qualités relationnelles et analytiques reconnues. Curieux, dynamique, vous faites preuve d'esprit d'équipe et vous pratiquez couramment l’anglais dans le cadre de vos missions (la pratique d’une seconde langue étrangère sera un plus). Vous êtes motivé par le challenge d’intervenir dans des contextes à fort enjeux stratégiques marqués par des opérations de haut de bilan et/ou de retournement et d’élargir vos compétences sur les dimensions IT, financières et opérationnelles.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/eight-advisory-sas/technology-transformation-senior-paris-393604","tags":["TF - T&T"],"job_types":["Manager","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Paris, Île-de-France, France","created_at":1793957465},{"slug":"gtm-recruiter-emea-paris-179672","company_name":"Notion","title":"GTM Recruiter, EMEA","description":"<h1>Who We Are</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is the collaborative AI workspace where teams and agents <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vkpYpWfEK5s">think together</a>. We're building one place where your knowledge, projects, meetings, and AI tools live side by side, so work is faster, clearer, and less fragmented. Millions of individuals, small teams, and large companies run their work on Notion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notinos (our employees) are customer zero in bringing this future of work to life. We care about craft, building things that last, and the belief that great work is still fundamentally human. Our goal isn’t to ship the next feature. Each and every team of Notinos is working to set the standard for how humans work together in the AI era. From building a business’s system of record to making and managing AI agents to automating away the busy work, we care deeply about giving our customers more time for their life’s work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>About the Role:</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Notion EMEA Recruiting team acts as trusted business partners who craft a thorough, inclusive, and curated interviewing experience. We believe hiring exceptional talent, at the right time, is the best path forward to achieve our company’s ambitious goals.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Go-to-Market Recruiter to support our growth across key Go-to-Market (GTM) teams in EMEA, with an emphasis on Sales. In this role, you'll help shape our recruiting strategy, manage full-cycle hiring efforts, and ensure a delightful yet rigorous hiring process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will be based in Paris. We work from our offices on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays (our Anchor Days) because we do our best thinking and building together in person. We’re looking for someone who’s excited to work alongside the team during those days. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What You'll Achieve:</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as a trusted recruiting partner to leaders across the GTM org, owning the full recruiting lifecycle from sourcing through successful close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and implement creative sourcing strategies to attract diverse top talent across EMEA markets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure scalable and structured hiring plans with consistent evaluation processes while creating thoughtful candidate experiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with cross-functional teams including Total Rewards, People Operations, and People Partners to drive holistic talent strategies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leverage AI tools, to innovate recruiting processes and provide data-driven insights on market conditions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion and scale best practices while thoughtfully adapting for regional nuances</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Skills You'll Need to Bring: </h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience in high-growth, technical, GTM functions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in French and English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of identifying, qualifying, and closing exceptional talent across various levels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience coaching and advising hiring managers through our recruiting process while keeping talent density as a priority</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to build diverse candidate pipelines and guide hiring managers in creating inclusive teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Outstanding communication, attention to detail, and interpersonal skills with a commitment to delivering high-quality recruiting experiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to thrive in fast-paced, dynamic environments</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Nice to Haves:</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passionate about leveraging technology and AI to transform recruiting processes</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is committed to providing highly competitive cash compensation, equity, and benefits. The compensation offered for this role will be based on multiple factors such as location, the role's scope and complexity, and the candidate's experience and expertise, and may vary from the range provided below. The estimated range for total on target earnings (including base salary and on target incentive pay) for this role is €98,000-€109,000 per year.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By clicking “Submit Application”, I understand and agree that Notion and its affiliates and subsidiaries will collect and process my information in accordance with Notion’s <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://notion.notion.site/Notion-Global-Recruiting-Privacy-Policy-fc3eb4e829354a26a2bb6fd5e289b550"><u>Global Recruiting Privacy Policy</u></a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://dev.notion.so/a3ce416456924276a59de91bca740028?pvs=21"><u>.</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Onsite</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>A Note on AI</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don’t need deep AI expertise for every role, but we do expect every Notino to be intellectually curious, drawn to tinkering and discovery, and excited to use AI as a real collaborator in their work. For some roles, AI fluency is a core requirement — when that’s the case, we'll say so explicitly in the qualifications. People who thrive here don’t treat AI as a novelty. They use it to think better, and make their work easier for others to build on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Equal Opportunity &amp; Accommodations</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire talented people from a wide range of backgrounds. If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every bullet, we still encourage you to apply. Notion is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of any legally protected characteristic. Consistent with applicable law, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records. Notion provides reasonable accommodations during the application process; if you need one, please let your recruiter know.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Notion is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate in hiring or any employment decision based on race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, genetic information, veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or other applicable legally protected characteristic. Notion considers qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Notion is also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, please let your recruiter know.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/0ac11447-a862-468b-95a0-40198c971382/5a7e80f3-d875-4693-938a-33455a593625" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/notion/gtm-recruiter-emea-paris-179672","tags":["People"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1793947211},{"slug":"enterprise-account-executive-med-france-136630","company_name":"Chainalysis","title":"Enterprise Account Executive - MED","description":"<h1>Enterprise Account Executive, TradFi &amp; Web3 Enterprise, MED (France &amp; Italy)</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Account Executives help organisations adopt digital assets with confidence by connecting their business needs to Chainalysis's blockchain intelligence solutions. They build trusted customer relationships, develop new business, and grow existing accounts through a consultative sales approach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an Enterprise Account Executive to cover France, Italy and Malta within our SEMEA team. Your primary focus will be two segments: traditional finance (TradFi), including retail, commercial, private and investment banks, payment and e-money institutions, and asset managers that are launching, supporting or exposed to digital asset activity; and the largest Web3 players, including major exchanges, brokers, custodians, stablecoin issuers and digital asset infrastructure providers operating at scale in France and Italy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own your territory strategy, navigate complex and highly regulated sales cycles, and engage stakeholders across compliance, financial crime, risk, security, procurement, digital assets and executive leadership, from bank CCOs to the compliance and security leaders of large crypto platforms. We measure success through quota attainment, new customer acquisition, and account growth across France and Italy.</p><h2>In this role, you'll</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceed your sales quota by acquiring new customers and growing existing accounts across France and Italy, with a primary focus on TradFi institutions and large Web3 enterprises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and execute territory and strategic account plans that reflect each market's banking and digital asset landscape, regulatory environment, and buying processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build relationships with decision-makers and champions across compliance, AML / financial crime, investigations, risk, security, digital assets teams, and executive leadership, in both TradFi and large Web3 organisations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and maintain a qualified pipeline through targeted prospecting, local industry relationships, partner collaboration (consultancies, advisory firms, technology partners), and customer referrals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead complex enterprise sales cycles from discovery through negotiation and close, working with customers' technical, legal, third-party risk, and procurement teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Connect Chainalysis solutions to customer outcomes, including managing exposure to crypto-asset service providers and their customers, meeting AML / CFT and sanctions obligations, supporting the safe launch and scaling of digital asset offerings, and investigating illicit activity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage customers on how MiCA, the Transfer of Funds Regulation (Travel Rule), DORA, EU AML rules and evolving French and Italian supervisory expectations affect their business needs, working with Chainalysis specialists where appropriate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Position Chainalysis as a partner for both worlds: help banks build confidence in digital assets, and help large Web3 players meet the compliance expectations of banks, regulators and institutional counterparties. Coordinate with the wider crypto native coverage to avoid overlap on mid-market and early-stage Web3 accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate forecasts and clear account plans, with consistent visibility into opportunities, risks, and next steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Solutions Engineering, Customer Success, Marketing, Partnerships, and other teams to develop proposals and support customer adoption.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Chainalysis at customer meetings and industry events across France and Italy, sharing market feedback to inform regional positioning and messaging.</p></li></ul><h2>We're looking for candidates who have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of B2B enterprise software or SaaS sales experience, including significant experience selling to banks or other regulated financial institutions (AML / financial crime, risk, compliance, fraud, or cybersecurity solutions) and/or to large crypto native organisations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A record of exceeding quota through consultative selling, new business development, and account growth in long, multi-stakeholder sales cycles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience developing enterprise accounts in France and/or Italy, with an understanding of local banking and Web3 market practices, procurement and vendor-onboarding processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid understanding of the crypto ecosystem and of the compliance, risk and security challenges facing both banks engaging with digital assets and large exchanges, custodians and infrastructure providers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to translate technical capabilities into clear business outcomes for different stakeholders, from compliance officers to CISOs to C-level executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using a structured enterprise sales methodology to qualify opportunities, develop customer champions, and manage complex deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and presentation skills, including the ability to engage senior executives and explain complex concepts clearly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional fluency in English and either French or Italian, with the ability to sell effectively across both markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to work independently across a defined territory while collaborating with regional and global teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A willingness to travel regularly across France and Italy and occasionally elsewhere in the SEMEA region.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional fluency in both French and Italian.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Established relationships within French and Italian banks, payment institutions, large crypto platforms, and financial services associations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling blockchain analytics, financial crime, KYC / transaction monitoring, fraud prevention, cybersecurity, or data analytics solutions to banks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with MiCA, the Travel Rule, DORA,European AML requirements, and the roles of relevant French and Italian authorities (e.g. ACPR, AMF, TRACFIN, Banca d'Italia, CONSOB, UIF).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling to banks launching digital asset services (custody, trading, tokenisation, stablecoins), or to large Web3 players serving institutional clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with local industry associations, advisory and Big 4 firms, and technology partners to develop a territory.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Chainalysis</strong><br />AI is not a feature at Chainalysis - it is a new way of working. One that turns instructions into work done, and helps us move faster than the threats we're built to counter, and we expect our employees to take ownership of the output and ensure quality. As the world's most trusted blockchain analytics platform, Chainalysis sits at a rare intersection of proprietary data, regulatory relationships and crypto expertise that makes it uniquely placed to shape and lead the next era of AI-driven intelligence - and we expect everyone here, regardless of role, to be an active part of it.<br /><br />AI fluency is tied directly to how we measure performance and how we plan to win. There is no substitute for your own curiosity. We provide the tools, workflows, and space to experiment - but the expectation is that you develop these capabilities yourself, bring ideas, and collaborate across teams to reinvent the way work gets done. We are not using AI to do less. We are using it to do what was never possible before.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Chainalysis</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Chainalysis is the blockchain data platform, making it easy to connect the movement of digital assets to real-world services. Powered by deep blockchain data and AI, organizations can investigate illicit activity, manage risk exposure, and develop innovative market solutions built on the industry's most trusted blockchain intelligence. Our mission is to build trust in blockchains, blending safety and security with an unwavering commitment to growth and innovation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You belong here. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Chainalysis, we believe that diversity of experience and thought makes us stronger. With both customers and employees around the world, we are committed to ensuring our team reflects the unique communities around us. We’re ensuring we keep learning by committing to continually revisit and reevaluate our diversity culture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We encourage applicants across any race, ethnicity, gender/gender expression, age, spirituality, ability, experience and more. If you need any accommodations to make our interview process more accessible to you due to a disability, don't hesitate to let us know. You can learn more <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://go.chainalysis.com/rs/503-FAP-074/images/Interview%20Accommodations%20Request.pdf">here</a>. We can’t wait to meet you. </p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/chainalysis/enterprise-account-executive-med-france-136630","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"France","created_at":1793947210},{"slug":"head-of-financial-controller-france-308115","company_name":"Filigran","title":"Head of Financial Controller","description":"<h2>🌀 The Company</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founded in 2022, Filigran is a global cybersecurity company on a mission to empower defense teams to be proactive through open-source solutions that uncover threats and drive action.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Filigran stands out in the cybersecurity ecosystem through its open-source, AI-powered and threat-informed approach to Continuous Threat Exposure Management (CTEM). Our eXtended Threat Management (XTM) platform brings together threat intelligence, exposure validation and cyber risk reduction, enabling organizations to better understand their threat landscape and take action.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the heart of Filigran is our open-source approach. Our vision is to unite defenders into a global community to make security more open, resilient and collaborative.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Filigran continues to scale globally, we are building the organization, infrastructure and capabilities needed for our next stage of growth. How we scale matters just as much as how fast we scale: our CORE values: Cohesion, Openness, Responsibility and Equity  shape how we work together, make decisions and build for the future.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>🎯 The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As <strong>Head of Financial Controller</strong>, you will own the full accounting function across Filigran's entities, including revenue recognition, consolidation, monthly and year-end close, and internal controls. You will act as the finance function's technical backbone building the infrastructure, controls, and processes needed to support a fast-scaling, multi-entity, international organization.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will report directly to the VP of Finance. The team is small so this role demands both strategic ownership and significant hands-on execution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>💼 Your Responsibilities</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>General Accounting Operations</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the accuracy, completeness, and timeliness of all financial transactions across Filigran entities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously improve a scalable monthly/quarterly close process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure revenue recognition is correctly applied and documented</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Multi-Entity Oversight</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead consolidation across Filigran's growing international entity structure (including new entity set-ups as the company expands)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the VP of Finance on transfer pricing, inter company transactions, and cross-border compliance matters</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Controls, Risk &amp; Governance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform ongoing gap analyses of accounting processes and proactively design and implement internal controls and policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the yearly financial audit end-to-end, acting as the primary point of contact for auditors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the relationship with the external accounting firm, holding them to a high standard of accuracy and responsiveness</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Systems &amp; Scalability</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to automate and streamline accounting workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build documentation that make the accounting function auditable and transferable</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leadership &amp; Cross-Functional Support</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a thought partner to the VP of Finance on technical accounting matters and process design</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage a current team of 3 general accountants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow the team to help support scalability and growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support ad hoc business requests, including finance topics adjacent to accounting (e.g., payroll coordination)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>🔎 Preferred Experience</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10+ years in accounting roles, including senior/lead or controller-level experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of French accounting standards; exposure to multi-GAAP/consolidation environments is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height