rade products meet rigorous operational standards before they are cleared for active duty.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working within a dedicated flight testing team, you will manage, prepare, and operate fleets of newly assembled drones or related product during intensive field validation campaigns. By logging massive operating hours, you will actively hunt for rare, hard-to-replicate system bugs and edge-case anomalies. We are looking for operators who combine rigorous testing discipline with the hands-on piloting expertise required to accurately assess and validate nominal drone behavior in flight. Your technical feedback will directly enable our engineering teams to secure and polish our next-generation defense systems.<br /></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intensive Flight Testing:</strong> Conduct high-volume flight testing of newly assembled interceptors to log hours, validate systems, and actively hunt for rare, intermittent flight anomalies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Aviation Performance Assessment:</strong> Manually operate, stress-test, and critically evaluate the flight dynamics of various platforms (multirotors, fixed-wing, flying wings, and RC planes) to ensure they handle exactly as designed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Field Deployment:</strong> Lead and execute demanding on-site flight missions, sometimes lasting several weeks, under diverse weather and environmental conditions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mission Safety &amp; Logs:</strong> Rigorously follow test checklists, maintain safety protocols during high-throughput flight operations, and accurately report flight observations to the engineering, production and industrialisation teams.<br /></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"