trong>Responsibilities</strong> </h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experiment Design &amp; Flight Test: Plan and run your own identification tests, from excitation design to flight tests, including coordinating with the .</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model Identification: Identify rigid-body, aerodynamic, propulsion and actuator dynamics using frequency and time-domain methods, including closed-loop identification on vehicles flown under a controller.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Propulsion &amp; Actuators: Characterize motors, ESCs, propellers and control surfaces, including bandwidth, delays, saturation, and thermal and battery effects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identification Pipeline: Build and maintain an automated, reproducible pipeline from flight logs to identified model. This covers ingestion, data-quality checks, estimation, validation and reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Model Validation: Validate models against held-out flight data, quantify uncertainty, and make sure each model is fit for purpose: controller design, simulation, or training learned G&amp;C.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">New Airframes: Extend the capability from multirotors to control-surface multirotors, fixed wings, tail-sitters and missiles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Simulation &amp; G&amp;C Support: Deliver models into simulation, SITL and HITL, and work closely with control, guidance and embedded engineers to close the loop between models and flight results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentorship: Depending on seniority, support the team by mentoring junior engineers and interns.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>Candidate Requirements</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Educational Background: A strong academic record with a degree in aerospace, control, mechanical engineering or a related STEM field. A practical track record matters more than the specific degree.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">System Identification: Proven experience identifying dynamic models of flying platforms from real data, in both the frequency and time domain, including the pitfalls of closed-loop data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flight Mechanics &amp; Control: Solid grasp of rigid-body dynamics, aerodynamic forces and moments, non-dimensionalization, stability modes and propulsion models. Also enough control background to know what the model will be used for.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flight Testing: Hands-on experience planning and running flight tests and working from raw, imperfect logs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software: Strong Python and scientific computing skills, with the discipline to build tools others can rerun.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3><strong>Nice to have </strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rigorous about data quality, uncertainty and validation; skeptical of models until they are proven.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Autonomous and hands-on, comfortable moving between bench, field and code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicates clearly, able to present models and test results to engineers and senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thrives under pressure in a fast-paced environment with a no-task-is-too-small mentality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fixed-wing aerodynamic modeling; VTOL or tail-sitter dynamics; remote pilot certification; experience with real flight logs; structural or vibration modes; data-driven or learned dynamics models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commitment: 100% dedication to Harmattan AI’s mission of providing a defensive edge to allied nations through ethical, high-impact technology.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/system-identification-engineer-lausanne-199944","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1793936415},{"slug":"electrical-distribution-engineer-zurich-456817","company_name":"Proxima Fusion GmbH","title":"Electrical Distribution Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO WE ARE</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proxima Fusion is Europe’s fastest-growing fusion company and the continent’s best-funded fusion player, as well as the first spin-out from the Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics (IPP). Backed by over €650M and powered by a growing team across Munich, Zurich, and Oxford, we are developing the hardware and infrastructure needed to deliver the world’s first commercial stellarator fusion power plant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our concept advances the most mature fusion technology out there, the Wendelstein 7-X stellarator, through two next-generation machines: Alpha and Stellaris. Our work combines stellarator optimization, advanced computation, machine learning, and high-temperature superconducting magnets to unlock higher-performance designs that were previously out of reach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turning these designs into a functioning fusion power plant requires excellence and ownership across every discipline, from physics and engineering to software, manufacturing, law, and business functions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>BY JOINING OUR TEAM YOU’LL GET TO</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Archi