ality, and protection coordination assessments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Specify and oversee the integration of electrical equipment, including transformers, switchgear, protection systems, and power conversion technologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish monitoring, diagnostics, and condition-based maintenance approaches to improve asset reliability and reduce unplanned downtime.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop predictive maintenance frameworks using operational and equipment health data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluate and develop opportunities for advanced grid services, including flexibility, ancillary services, demand response, and other emerging market offerings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore innovative digital and online services that can enhance plant performance, operational visibility, and value creation within future energy systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO YOU ARE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a University (Higher education) degree in Electrical Engineering, Control Systems, Computer Science or equivalent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a strong background in electrical engineering, control systems, or a related field, with hands-on experience in industrial environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are adaptable and motivated to grow with evolving technologies and increasing system complexity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in grid integration, or electrical infrastructure for industrial, utility-scale, or energy-related facilities is a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of reactive power compensation is a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>INTERVIEW PROCESS</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruiter I