&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/nebius/service-desk-l3-it-operations-technical-lead-amsterdam-139561","tags":["IT Operations"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793948121},{"slug":"devops-engineer-amsterdam-449903","company_name":"SkinVision","title":"DevOps Engineer","description":"<p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">For this role, we will only consider candidates who are currently based in the Netherlands.</span></span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">About SkinVision</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Skin cancer is highly treatable when caught early, but limited access to specialist care and long wait times delay diagnosis, increasing the risk of late-stage cases and driving up treatment costs. SkinVision, founded in Amsterdam in 2012, exists to close that gap. Our proprietary AI — certified as a Class IIa medical device under EU regulation, with over 90% sensitivity and 89% specificity — has already helped nearly 3 million people worldwide detect early signs of skin cancer. Today, SkinVision has a database of more than 6 million skin spot assessments and can reach 20 million people through insurer partnerships. High-risk cases are reviewed by a team of dermatologists, who support users in taking the right next step — from urgent care to a specialist referral. We are extending this further, connecting users faster to the specialist care they need. We're a focused, international team, active globally, united by one goal: making early detection accessible to everyone, everywhere. If you join us, you're not just building a product — you're helping close the gap between a person noticing something and getting the care they need.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">DevOps at SkinVision</span></span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">As a DevOps Engineer at SkinVision, you will play a key role in building, scaling, and securing the infrastructure that powers our AI-driven health platform. You’ll design and maintain our cloud-based systems in AWS, implement CI/CD pipelines, enhance observability using Datadog, and drive operational excellence through automation and monitoring.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Your work will directly impact the reliability and scalability of a medical-grade system that serves users globally. You’ll collaborate closely with backend, ML, and product teams to ensure smooth delivery, rapid deployments, and resilient operations — ultimately enabling us to deliver life-saving technology with confidence.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Beyond hands-on expertise with AWS and modern DevOps tooling, we’re looking for someone who thinks architecturally. You’ll get to know our current setup, form your own view of how it should evolve, and help define a target vision for our infrastructure, then drive its implementation. Day-to-day operational work is part of the role, but we value someone who thinks before building and takes ownership of where our infrastructure goes next.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.1em"><span style="color:#121317">What you will do</span></span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Cloud Infrastructure &amp; Automation</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Design, build, and manage AWS-based infrastructure, ensuring high availability, scalability, and cost efficiency.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Implement and manage infrastructure as code (IaC) using tools like Terraform or CloudFormation.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Automate environment provisioning, configuration, and deployments using CI/CD pipelines.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Ensure system resilience, security, and performance through automated monitoring and alerting.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">CI/CD &amp; Deployment</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Design and optimize CI/CD pipelines to support rapid, reliable, and safe deployments across environments.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Manage deployment workflows using Argo CD and Kubernetes.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Collaborate with developers and ML engineers to streamline build, test, and release processes.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Integrate automated testing, rollback strategies, and version control into the deployment lifecycle.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Observability &amp; Monitoring</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Build a comprehensive observability stack using Datadog for metrics, logs, traces, and alerts.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Define service-level objectives (SLOs), service-level indicators (SLIs), and dashboards for system performance.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Proactively detect and resolve performance bottlenecks, capacity issues, and reliability risks.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Create automated health checks and ensure visibility across production systems.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Security &amp; Compliance</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Implement security best practices for AWS, containers, and CI/CD pipelines.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Manage identity, access, and secret handling (IAM, Secrets Manager, Parameter Store).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Ensure compliance with medical device standards and data privacy regulations (GDPR, HIPAA).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Partner with the Information Security Officer to embed security controls across infrastructure and deployments.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Reliability &amp; Incident Management</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Lead incident response and root cause analysis for infrastructure or deployment-related issues.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Establish SLAs and operational runbooks for production environments.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Continuously improve system reliability through chaos testing, redundancy, and fault tolerance.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Mentor engineers on DevOps principles, observability practices, and infrastructure automation.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Infrastructure Strategy &amp; Architecture</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Assess the current infrastructure and deployment setup, and form a well-reasoned view of how it should evolve.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Define and maintain a target architecture for our cloud platform, balancing reliability, scalability, security, and cost.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Translate the target vision into a practical roadmap and drive its implementation incrementally, alongside day-to-day operations.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Document and communicate architectural decisions, aligning with engineering and leadership on technical direction.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Essential skills</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Minimum of 6 years of experience in DevOps, Site Reliability Engineering, or Cloud Infrastructure roles.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Stro