et cijfers om in acties en verbeteringen.</p></li><li><p>Je bent proactief, bouwt sterke interne netwerken op en realiseert je doelen.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><h2>Over DPD Nederland</h2><p>Met 12 depots in Nederland en als onderdeel van Geopost, zijn we verbonden met een internationaal netwerk dat jaarlijks 1,2 miljard pakketten verwerkt. Achter deze indrukwekkende cijfers staan duizenden collega’s die zich elke dag inzetten, straks samen met jou.</p><p>Onze cultuur is ondernemend, betrouwbaar en mensgericht. Wat ooit begon als een nuchter MKB-bedrijf leeft nog steeds voort: praktisch, sociaal en trots. We geloven in persoonlijk contact, samenwerking en zelf aanpakken. Uitdagingen gaan we niet uit de weg. Dat zit in ons DNA.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>We groeien hard, hebben grote ambities en <strong>jij hoort er straks écht bij. Samen maken we het verschil.</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><h2>Solliciteren</h2><p><strong>Solliciteer eenvoudig via onderstaande sollicitatiebutton.</strong> Wij nemen zo snel mogelijk contact met je op. Zijn we allebei enthousiast? Dan zetten we samen de volgende stappen in de sollicitatieprocedure.</p><ol><li><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong>Kennismaking: </strong>w<em>e leren elkaar beter kennen tijdens een eerste gesprek.</em></p></li><li><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong>Assessment: </strong><em>je maakt een online assessment thuis.</em></p></li><li><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong>Tweede gesprek: </strong><em>we bespreken de resultaten en gaan verder in op de functie.</em></p></li><li><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <strong>Aanbod: </strong><em>is er een match? Dan doen we je graag een aanbod.</em></p></li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Vragen? Neem gerust contact op met onze corporate recruiter, Donne van der Wal via +31 6 &nbsp;29 989 532.</p><p>Klik <u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://werkenbijdpd.nl/ons-sollicitatieproces">hier</a></u> voor meer informatie over ons sollicitatieproces.</p><p><br><strong><em>Acquisitie en doorplaatsing van deze vacature worden niet op prijs gesteld.</em></strong></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/dpd/teamleider-sales-support-strategic-accounts-eindhoven-365906","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Entry","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Eindhoven, Noord-Brabant, Nederland","created_at":1793935911},{"slug":"devops-engineer-amsterdam-263780","company_name":"Intelic","title":"DevOps Engineer","description":"<p>In a world where geopolitical tensions and security threats are accelerating, the way nations protect people and preserve peace is being redefined. For a long time, innovating in defense was about making tougher hardware. But with the evolution of software and the recent AI disruption, the future of defense is shifting to software-powered unmanned systems that save lives by removing humans from the front line. This is our mission.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>At Intelic, we're building the intelligence layer for unmanned systems in defense. As a software-first company, we enable autonomous platforms to operate together - faster, smarter, and more reliably - across complex, mission-critical environments. Our technology turns disconnected assets into coordinated forces, helping operators make accurate decisions when it matters most.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Based in Amsterdam and growing fast, Intelic offers a rare opportunity to work on products that don't just move metrics - they meaningfully impact safety, resilience, and the future of Europe's security.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Why This Role Exists</h3><p>Nexus has to run in places most software never goes: offline, in the field, installed and operated by people who are not developers. Getting it there in one piece, and keeping it running, is a job on its own.</p><p>Right now that job sits mostly with three backend engineers who cover this alongside their own work. As Nexus grows, so does the team, and we're adding someone to take real ownership of the pipelines, installers, and infrastructure that turn Nexus into something operators can trust, and who treats security as part of how the work gets done, not a separate project bolted on afterwards.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>What You Will Do</h3><p>You will join Product Adoption, the team that owns the last stretch between working software and a field-ready product: deployment, installers, monitoring, and everything that keeps Nexus running once it leaves the building. We are hiring at medior to senior level, roughly a 2 to 3, with room to flex higher for the right person.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>Build and maintain the CI/CD pipelines that turn Nexus into an installable, field-ready product across Linux and Windows</p></li><li><p>Maintain and harden our software supply chain, including dependency scanning and package security</p></li><li><p>Own the Windows installer and service orchestration, and help developers debug the platform-specific issues that come with it: permissions, firewalls, services, "works on my machine"</p></li><li><p>Secure the software update server, the one online touchpoint in an otherwise offline system, and keep telemetry from the field reliable without leaking sensitive data</p></li><li><p>Harden APIs and authentication on the surfaces that face the outside world</p></li><li><p>Maintain and gradually take over our on-prem infrastructure: physical servers, backups, and disaster recovery, as we move away from renting machines in the cloud</p></li><li><p>Build small internal tools, mostly in Python, Rust and shell or PowerShell scripts: installers, updaters, and the occasional internal or customer-facing web app</p></li><li><p>Support incident response when things break in production, and help build the monitoring that catches problems before customers do</p></li><li><p>Write down what you learn, so the next person, including future you, doesn't have to debug the same thing twice</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h3>You'll Thrive Here If</h3><ul><li><p>You bring solid experience with CI/CD pipelines and build automation</p></li><li><p>Comfort working across both Linux and Windows, with the ability to actually debug problems on either, not just deploy to them</p></li><li><p>Experience with infrastructure as code (Ansible, OpenTofu, or similar)</p></li><li><p>A security mindset: hardening, secure defaults, and attack surface are just part of how you build things, not an afterthought</p></li><li><p>Enough scripting or programming ability to read and contribute to Python, Rust, or shell scripts. There is there is plenty of custom tooling to build.</p></li><li><p>A level head under pressure. You can prioritise and stay steady when a few things break at once</p></li></ul><p><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Experience with on-prem, bare-metal or virtulized infrastructure, not just cloud consoles</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with Docker</p></li><li><p>Exposure to dependency and package scanning tools such as Sonatype</p></li><li><p>An interest in platform or infrastructure engineering as its own discipline. We expect this to split into a dedicated function over time</p></li><li><p>Ability to build in-house tooling where needed and integrate vendor solutions where they fit</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h3>What Your First Year Will Look Like</h3><ul><li><p>You've taken over meaningful parts of the CI/CD pipeline and installer work independently, without needing step-by-step instructions</p></li><li><p>You've hardened at least one exposed surface end to end, the update server, an API, or similar</p></li><li><p>You've helped move part of our infrastructure off rented machines and onto hardware we run ourselves</p></li><li><p>Developers come to you when something breaks on Windows or Linux, because you've built a track record of finding the actual root cause</p></li><li><p>You've documented enough of what you know that the team is less dependent on any one person, including you</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h3>Why Intelic</h3><ul><li><p>We are setting up an environment, largely from the ground up that has to approved by MoDs</p></li><li><p>You won't be bored. New projects, new problems, and a steady stream of things nobody has solved here before</p></li><li><p>Real ownership from day one, not ticket-taking. If you see a better tool or approach, you're free to try it</p></li><li><p>You'll work with hardware that matters: servers you can walk up to, deployments running in places with no internet, problems that cloud-only engineers rarely see</p></li><li><p>A small team that leans on each other. When someone's on leave, the rest pick up the slack, and vice versa</p></li><li><p>The mission is real. Nexus supports operators in the field, and how well you build and secure it has a direct effect on whether it works when it counts</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>What We Offer</h3><ul><li><p>Stock Appreciation Rights programme (equity)</p></li><li><p>A vibrant office at NDSM Plein, Amsterdam Noord — where we come together in person every day, because we believe it matters for the kind of work we do</p></li><li><p>Flexible pension plan</p></li><li><p>25 vacation days</p></li><li><p>Travel allowance</p></li><li><p>Urban Sports corporate membership</p></li><li><p>Lease a Bike option</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>Please note that, as part of our recruitment process, we may request a Certificate of Conduct (VOG) and conduct a background screening in accordance with our screening policy. We appreciate your understanding and cooperation throughout this process.</em></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/intelic/devops-engineer-amsterdam-263780","tags":[],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793935911},{"slug":"senior-backend-engineer-rust-amsterdam-74770","company_name":"Intelic","title":"Senior Backend Engineer (Rust)","description":"<h3><strong>About Intelic</strong></h3><p>In a world where geopolitical tensions and security threats are accelerating, the way nations protect people and preserve peace is being redefined. At Intelic, we're building the intelligence layer for unmanned systems in defense: software that enables autonomous platforms to operate together, faster, smarter, and more reliably, across complex, mission-critical environments.</p><p>Based in Amsterdam and growing fast, we offer a rare opportunity to work on products that don't just move metrics. They directly affect safety, resilience, and Europe's security.</p><h3><strong>Why the role exists</strong></h3><p>Our drones carry more and more hardware: cameras, gimbals, servos and more. The European market is fragmented, so we need to support many different types of hardware. Right now, adding a new piece of hardware usually means our own engineers have to integrate it. We want to change that. We're building a platform that lets partners and other teams connect their own hardware and write their own driver.</p><p>You'll work alongside robotics engineers and help set the team up from the start. The APIs and system design you create will be what everyone else builds on.</p><p>If you like hard backend problems where good design directly affects how fast other people can move, this role is worth a look.</p><h3><strong>What you will do</strong></h3><p>You'll spend most of your time in Rust, working out how to abstract the communication with the hardware from the rest of the system. That could mean designing how a new camera gets configured through the API, or writing a simulated camera so you can test an integration before the hardware is on your desk.</p><ul><li><p>Design and build the platform in Rust</p></li><li><p>Define the APIs that other teams and partners use to integrate cameras, gimbals, servos and other hardware</p></li><li><p>Make it possible for others to write their own drivers and add hardware without needing support from your team</p></li><li><p>Think through how each new module fits into the wider system, and plan for the cases others will run into later</p></li><li><p>Write strong unit tests and add integration tests, including tests against simulated hardware</p></li><li><p>Work directly with other teams to understand what they need from the platform and agree on how systems talk to each other</p></li><li><p>Help set up the team, and hand it over well once the platform is in good shape</p></li></ul><h3><strong>You will thrive here if</strong></h3><ul><li><p>You have around five or more years of engineering experience in a heavy backend language. Rust is ideal, C++ or similar also works</p></li><li><p>You've built platforms or APIs that other teams depend on, and you think about how your part fits into the larger system</p></li><li><p>You work independently. You take a problem, work it out with the team, and see it through without someone managing every step</p></li><li><p>You talk to people. You reach out to other teams, ask questions, and don't wait for work to come to you</p></li><li><p>You take testing seriously, and you know how to test code that talks to hardware</p></li><li><p>You use AI coding tools like Claude in your day to day work</p></li><li><p>You enjoy technical problems more than product decisions. Here, what needs to be built is fairly clear. The job is to build it well</p></li></ul><p><strong>Bonus if you have:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Basic hardware knowledge: you know how to power a camera and get video out of it</p></li><li><p>Experience with drones, robotics or other connected hardware</p></li></ul><h3><strong>How we work</strong></h3><p>We're a startup, so we plan about three months ahead and things can change after that. The team you join is small and may not stay in its current form forever. Once the platform is set up, you may move on to work on the wider vehicle platform.</p><ul><li><p>Strong unit testing is the standard. Integration tests are added where they make sense, often using simulated hardware</p></li><li><p>Other teams build on your APIs and integrate their own hardware, so you don't have to do every integration yourself</p></li><li><p>Engineers work directly with other teams to agree on interfaces</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What your first year will look like</strong></h3><p>At 6 months: You own this part of the system. The platform is set up, and the team is working at the level you helped set.</p><p>At 12 months: The platform runs without you in the middle of it, and you're helping on the wider vehicle platform, including the flight side.</p><h3><strong>Why Intelic</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>The mission is real.</strong> We're building technology that makes Europe safer.</p></li><li><p><strong>Your work multiplies.</strong> Set the platform up well, and every team can integrate new hardware without waiting on anyone.</p></li><li><p><strong>You build it from the start.</strong> You shape the APIs and the team instead of maintaining someone else's design.</p></li><li><p><strong>You can focus on engineering.</strong> The problem is clear. Your job is to solve it well.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What we offer</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Stock Appreciation Rights program</p></li><li><p>Travel allowance</p></li><li><p>Flexible pension plan</p></li><li><p>25 vacation days</p></li><li><p>Urban Sports Club membership</p></li><li><p>Bike lease through 'Lease a Bike'</p></li><li><p>A modern office at NDSM Plein, Amsterdam Noord. We value working shoulder to shoulder, so we're in the office 4 days a week. You also get 10 days a year to work from wherever you want.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em><span style="color:#5A5F72">Please note that, as part of our recruitment process, we may request a Certificate of Conduct (VOG) and conduct a background screening in accordance with our screening policy. We appreciate your understanding and cooperation throughout this process.</span></em></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/intelic/senior-backend-engineer-rust-amsterdam-74770","tags":[],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793935911},{"slug":"backend-engineer-amsterdam-1468","company_name":"Inner Circle","title":"Backend Engineer","description":"<p><em><span style="color:#000000">Engineering · Amsterdam (hybrid)</span></em><strong><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Inner Circle is a dating app for people who are done wasting time. Every member is screened thoroughly, so the profiles you see are people worth dating.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Every AI-powered feature starts with the data and infrastructure behind it. From building scalable backend systems to powering smarter matching and personalisation, our engineers turn data into meaningful connections - and shape how AI transforms the future of dating.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Goal of the Role</span></strong><br></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You power the engine that brings more members together every second. We’re moving our backend from a PHP monolith to Kotlin services, and changing how we build software at the same time: AI and agentic engineering are part of how our team works every day. You’ll join the team building the new part of our system, and occasionally work in our legacy PHP codebase.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You don’t need prior PHP or Kotlin experience. We care more about how you think and approach problems than about which language you have used so far.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Tech stack: Kotlin, Spring Boot, GraphQL, PHP 8 (legacy), MySQL (Aurora), Redis, OpenSearch, RabbitMQ, Docker, Kubernetes (EKS), AWS (S3, SNS/SQS, SES, Rekognition, and more), DataDog</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Result Areas:</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Build and ship features that matter to members</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Deliver backend features that improve matchmaking, engagement and retention. You work from outcome-based stories: the team agrees on the result, and you own how to get there.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Help move our platform to Kotlin services</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Build new Kotlin services and help extract functionality from the PHP monolith step by step, without disrupting the members who use the app every day.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Work with AI, and with judgement</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Use AI and agentic tools such as Claude Code in your daily work. Give them clear specs and context, and review what they produce as critically as you would review a colleague’s code.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Own the quality of what you build</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Write clean, testable code with automated tests, keep pull requests small, follow secure coding practices, and stay responsible for your code once it runs in production.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Make pragmatic trade-offs</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Reason through problems and ship solutions that are good enough. Recognise when something needs more care or optimisation, and ask for input when a decision is bigger than your part of the system.</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#000000">What you bring:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">3+ years of experience in backend engineering</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Proficiency in at least one typed backend language, such as Kotlin, Java, C#, Go, TypeScript or PHP</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Solid experience with APIs and relational databases, including query performance</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Understanding of systems design and software architecture, and the ability to reason about trade-offs</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You know why clean code matters and you apply it, with or without AI</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience writing automated tests and working with CI/CD</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Hands-on experience with AI coding tools, or a strong drive to learn agentic engineering practices</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Clear communication in English, both spoken and written (design docs, decision records, pull request descriptions)</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Nice to have:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience with AWS</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience with event-driven systems or microservice architectures</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Familiarity with Domain-Driven Design or clean architecture</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience with Kotlin or the JVM</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience working in, and gradually migrating, a legacy codebase</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">You:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Curious, and keen to try new tools and ways of working</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Focused on outcomes rather than output</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Pragmatic: you know when good enough is good enough</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Comfortable asking questions and explaining your reasoning</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">An authentic team player</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">What we offer:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A fulltime job that makes a positive impact on people's lives</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A competitive salary matched with your experience and ambition</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">An amazing work environment in our office at Prins Hendrikkade, at the heart of Amsterdam</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A Macbook or other hardware of your choice to be able to do your job</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Stay healthy and bring your own device allowance</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Training and development budget</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Frequent team get-togethers and team activities</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Free Inner Circle VIP membership for you and your single friends</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">About Inner Circle</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Inner Circle is a dating app built on the contrarian belief: opposites don't attract. The best connections happen between people who already live life the same way. So we don't sell more options, or better odds. We sell relevance, people worth dating. Every member is screened, so effort and intention are in place before anyone gets in. And where every other app is built to keep you swiping, ours is built to get you off it, and onto a date with someone worth your time.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="color:#000000">At Inner Circle, we embrace our diverse community and team. We celebrate differences and know that they are key for helping us grow. Our team consists of 40 team members, with 16 nationalities and a female: male ratio of 60 : 40. Whatever your race, religion, colour, gender, national origin, political affiliation, sexual orientation, marital status, disability or age, we make sure everyone has the space to be themselves.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Ready to make an impact? Let's get the ball rolling, apply now.</span></strong></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/inner-circle/backend-engineer-amsterdam-1468","tags":["Tech & Product"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1793935911},{"slug":"senior-tech-talent-partner-amsterdam-267674","company_name":"The Rec Hub","title":"Senior Tech Talent Partner - Amsterdam","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 <strong>Senior Talent Partner - Technology</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📄 Fixed Term Contract - 6 months</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📍Hybrid - Amsterdam - 3 days in office</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring a Talent Acquisition Partner to support one of our clients with their technology hiring. You'll need to know how to hire technical people (think software engineers and product) for a global technology organisation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be a true partner to the business, sourcing top talent, optimising processes, and delivering quality hires fast. Your work will be very visible as part of our delivery team for this client.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌟 What You’ll Do:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own end-to-end hiring across several key business areas</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the data as we hire, looking for more than just activity - helping managers make better decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build trusted partnerships with hiring managers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source top talent through creative and strategic methods</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver a seamless, high-quality candidate experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive continuous improvement in how we hire</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help build out recruitment strategies that will support hiring over the next 12 to 24 months</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔍 What You Bring:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>5+ years</strong> in full-cycle recruitment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record in Tech hiring in fast paced environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident working independently and managing stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on sourcing experience across passive and active talent pools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driven, adaptable, and outcomes-focused</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build real trust with our client</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/the-rec-hub/senior-tech-talent-partner-amsterdam-267674","tags":["Partnerships & Delivery"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam - Hybrid","created_at":1793925611},{"slug":"enterprise-account-executive-benelux-flexible-netherlands-443116","company_name":"Sysdig","title":"Enterprise Account Executive (BeNeLux)","description":"<p>At Sysdig, we believe cloud security isn't a compromise - it's a promise. From the start, our mission has been clear: to help organizations secure innovation in the cloud, the right way.</p>
<p>We created Falco, the open standard for cloud threat detection, and continue to lead the cloud security market with runtime insights, open innovation, and agentic Al. Creators of technology trusted by over 60% of the Fortune 500, Sysdig gives teams the real-time clarity to move fast and defend what matters most.</p>
