 is building its investment business from Vilnius. As General Manager of Doit Lithuania, you will build and run the business in Lithuania and grow it across the European Economic Area.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the first senior hire in Lithuania. You will own the regulatory relationship, the build of the team, the partner network and the launch. You will sit on the management board and lead the business day to day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a generalist who learns quickly, thinks deeply, and enjoys solving difficult problems in a fast-moving, regulated environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Own</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the relationship with the Bank of Lithuania and other regulators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the Vilnius team, including compliance, operations and control functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Select and negotiate with execution, custody, fund and banking partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the business plan, financial projections, capital plan and budget.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launch the investment platform in Lithuania and roll it out across the EEA.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up governance, policies and controls that meet EU and Lithuanian requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with group leadership on product, engineering and growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report to the board and take ownership of business and regulatory outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generalist background in consulting, investment banking, start-ups, private equity or venture capital.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or scaling a business, ideally in financial services or fintech.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong problem-solving skills and business judgment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to learn regulation quickly and work credibly with regulators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong ownership and execution skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with boards, regulators, partners and teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working across product, operations, finance and compliance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clean record and good reputation, suitable for regulatory approval as a senior manager.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Lithuania, or open to relocating to Lithuania.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curious, resourceful, and driven to build.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lithuanian language ability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An existing working relationship with the Bank of Lithuania.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with MiFID II, brokerage, wealth management or fund distribution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or running a regulated financial business in the EU.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This Role Is Not For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People who only want to attend meetings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Candidates who cannot follow up aggressively and professionally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Those who need fixed scope and slow timelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People who avoid messy cross-functional problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">People who produce long updates withou