ant to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we work</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-velocity: </strong>Rapid experimentation, lean autonomous teams, and minimal bureaucracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact not job titles: </strong>We don’t have job titles. Instead, it’s about the impact you have. No task is above or beneath you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI first:</strong> We use AI to move faster with higher-quality results. We do this across the whole company—from engineering to growth to operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence everywhere: </strong>Everything we do should match the quality of our AI models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global team: </strong>We prioritize your talent, not your location.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovative culture:</strong> You’ll be part of a generational opportunity to define the trajectory of AI, surrounded by a team pushing the boundaries of what’s possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth paths: </strong>Joining ElevenLabs means joining a dynamic team with countless opportunities to drive impact - beyond your immediate role and responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; development</strong>: ElevenLabs proactively supports professional development through an annual discretionary stipend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Social travel</strong>: We also provide an annual discretionary stipend to meet up with colleagues each year, however you choose.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual team offsite: </strong>Each year, we bring your entire team together in a new location - past offsites have included Croatia, Italy and Cancún</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Co-working</strong>: If you’re not located near one of our main hubs, we offer a monthly co-working stipend.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>About the role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs has grown to over 1,000 in three years, and the rate of growth is not slowing down. As Talent Lead, you will be in charge of one of the most visible and impactful functions in the company: hundreds of hires a quarter across Research, Engineering, GTM and Operations, in one of the most competitive talent markets in history. You’ll move Talent from a high-volume recruiting engine to a strategic partner that tells leaders what is achievable, and you’ll rebuild how we hire using the same AI products we make.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll run the entire Talent team (currently 20 - 30 recruiters, sourcers, and talent operations) across verticals, setting the strategy, building the systems, and staying hands-on where it matters. You'll report directly to the Operations Lead and be a close partner to the People team. This isn't a pure executive role - we want someone who still loves the craft of recruiting and can model what great looks like for the team around them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The right person has done this before at scale - at a company that grew fast and hired harder. Your team will look to you not just for direction, but as someone they can genuinely learn from. This will be an opportunity to shape the direction of Talent at ElevenLab; where we go, how we get there and who we get there with. If you want to shape the future of the Talent industry by building industry-defining playbooks using the latest technology and AI solutions, whilst building an expert team - this might be your best fit yet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the full talent function across Research, GTM, Engineering &amp; Product, and G&amp;A hiring - setting strategy, managing team performance, building a recruiter capacity engine, and driving outcomes across all verticals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape Talent Operations: ATS (Ashby) configuration, headcount tracking, hiring velocity metrics, and recruiter tooling - ensuring the function runs with precision and minimal friction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify innovative ways of approaching Talent: design the next-gen Talent org structure, envision how Talent processes can be agentified and work with the team to build ElevenLabs products throughout.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a strategic partner to department heads and hiring managers, bringing market intelligence, pipeline health visibility, and honest counsel on what it takes to consistently win the best people in the market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a strong talent brand through thoughtful candidate experience, community engagement, building a Talent events program and creative sourcing strategies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach and develop a team of recruiters, establishing clear standards for quality of hire, speed, and candidate experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with functional leaders across Research, Engineering, GTM, and Operations - acting as a trusted advisor who can challenge, align, and mobilize leaders around talent priorities and workforce strategy.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re moving quickly on this search. Applications close on 13 November 2026, and we’ll start reviewing right away, so we’d encourage you to apply early.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Requirements</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record leading large TA functions at high-growth companies, with direct experience filling hundreds of roles per year across multiple functions and geographies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on recruiting instincts - comfortable being in the weeds on critical searches, not just managing from a distance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong people leader who builds, develops, and retains recruiting talent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharp on process: able to design and iterate on systems, tooling, and workflows that make a team of 20–30 perform at a high level with AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close collaborator with People, Finance, and business leaders - comfortable operating at the intersection of headcount planning, compensation, and hiring strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Held a high bar for quality of hire while hitting aggressive volume, with the metrics to show it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advised founders and executive suite on workforce planning, and changed a plan with your judgment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Worked with Finance, People and RevOps on headcount planning, capacity modelling, compensation and offer strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has recruited across the Americas, EMEA and APAC and understands the differences between markets.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Location</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is remote-first, so it can be executed from anywhere, with the ability to operate from New York or London strongly preferred. If you prefer, you can work from our offices in London, New York, San Francisco, and Warsaw.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Remote</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability or other legally protected statuses.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/elevenlabs/talent-lead-london-269575","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793947213},{"slug":"billing-operations-manager-london-5454","company_name":"Elevenlabs","title":"Billing Operations Manager","description":"<h2>About ElevenLabs</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs is an AI research and product company transforming how we interact with technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in January 2023 with the first human-like AI voice model. Today, we serve millions of users and thousands of businesses - from fast-growing startups to large enterprises like Deutsche Telekom and Meta. Our investors are some of the world's most prominent, including Andreessen Horowitz, ICONIQ Growth and Sequoia. We've raised $781M in funding and our last valuation was $22B - multiples of 11, always.<br /><br />We have expanded from voice into three main platforms:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAgents enables businesses to deliver seamless and intelligent customer experiences, with the integrations, testing, monitoring, and reliability necessary to deploy voice and chat agents at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenCreative empowers creators and marketers to generate and edit speech, music, image, and video across 70+ languages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenAPI gives developers access to our leading AI audio foundational models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everything we do is the result of the creativity and commitment of our team - builders doing the best work of their lives. We are researchers, engineers, and operators. IOI medalists and ex-founders. If you want to work hard and create lasting positive impact, we want to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we work</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-velocity: </strong>Rapid experimentation, lean autonomous teams, and minimal bureaucracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact not job titles: </strong>We don’t have job titles. Instead, it’s about the impact you have. No task is above or beneath you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI first:</strong> We use AI to move faster with higher-quality results. We do this across the whole company—from engineering to growth to operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Excellence everywhere: </strong>Everything we do should match the quality of our AI models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global team: </strong>We prioritize your talent, not your location.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovative culture:</strong> You’ll be part of a generational opportunity to define the trajectory of AI, surrounded by a team pushing the boundaries of what’s possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth paths: </strong>Joining ElevenLabs means joining a dynamic team with countless opportunities to drive impact - beyond your immediate role and responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; development</strong>: ElevenLabs proactively supports professional development through an annual discretionary stipend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Social travel</strong>: We also provide an annual discretionary stipend to meet up with colleagues each year, however you choose.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual team offsite: </strong>Each year, we bring your entire team together in a new location - past offsites have included Croatia, Italy and Cancún</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Co-working</strong>: If you’re not located near one of our main hubs, we offer a monthly co-working stipend.</p></li></ul><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">ElevenLabs is scaling fast – new enterprise customers, new products, new markets. The Billing Operations Specialist is the person who makes sure every deal that closes is reflected correctly in our systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an operational ownership role, sitting at the intersection of Sales, Customer Success, Finance, and Engineering – responsible for the full billing lifecycle of our enterprise accounts, from provisioning a new customer on day one to cleanly closing out a churned account. You'll resolve discrepancies before customers notice them, catch configuration drift before it becomes a revenue problem, and build the processes that make billing feel invisible to everyone else. You'll also work on projects and programs that evolve the sophistication of our billing processes and our tooling, and help with things like pricing migrations and other critical efforts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ideal person is someone who is obsessive about accuracy and automation, comfortable navigating ambiguity, and energized (not frustrated) by the complexity of managing billing at scale across thousands of accounts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provisioning</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate closed-won deals from Salesforce into correctly configured subscriptions in our billing platforms, such as Stripe – pricing plan, billing interval, contract start date, trial periods, discounts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the reconciliation between executed order forms and what's been requested for provisioning; work with Sales and Legal to resolve any gaps</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Engineering to identify automation opportunities and build guardrails that make provisioning faster and more accurate over time</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Subscription &amp; account management</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Process mid-cycle changes and manage renewal mechanics – upgrades, downgrades, seat changes, plan switches, and so on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle offboarding cleanly: close subscriptions, issue final invoices or credits, ensure no residual billing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Resolve invoice discrepancies raised by customers or flagged by the Customer Success team – incorrect amounts, missing credits, misapplied discounts</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Revenue integrity</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run periodic audits of active subscriptions to verify billing matches contracted terms</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and remediate ghost subscriptions, duplicate customers, and orphaned invoices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support month-end and quarter-end close by reconciling billing platforms with Finance's records</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Surface pricing or configuration anomalies to relevant teams.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must-have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2-5 years in billing operations, revenue operations, finance operations or a similar role supporting B2B or enterprise customers (adjust the range for level)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with a subscription billing platform, ideally Stripe Billing or similar (Chargebee, Zuora, Recurly), including subscriptions, invoices, credits, coupons and billing intervals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience turning closed-won deals and order forms into correct billing configurations (pricing plan, start date, trial, discounts)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong attention to detail and a record of catching discrepancies before customers do</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can read a contract or order form and spot gaps against what was requested for provisioning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience reconciling billing data to finance records, including supporting month-end or quarter-end close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working with Salesforce (or another CRM) as the source of truth for deals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear written communication and ability to work across Sales, Customer Success, Finance, Legal and Engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with ambiguity and with managing a high volume of accounts without losing track</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong plus</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with usage-based or hybrid pricing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with SQL, spreadsheets at scale (pivots, lookups), or BI tools, for audits and reconciliation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building automation or scripts, or partnering with Engineering on guardrails (APIs, webhooks, no-code tools)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running subscription audits, such as finding ghost subscriptions, duplicate customers and orphaned invoices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with pricing migrations or billing-system migrations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to ASC 606 or revenue recognition basics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with a quote-to-cash stack (CPQ, contract management, ERP such as NetSuite)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience at a high-growth SaaS or AI company</p></li></ul><h2>Location</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is remote-first, so it can be executed from anywhere in the United States or Europe. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-remote</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, disability or other legally protected statuses.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/elevenlabs/billing-operations-manager-london-5454","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793947213},{"slug":"flight-ticketing-and-disruption-manager-london-30045","company_name":"loveholidays","title":"Flight Ticketing and Disruption Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why loveholidays? <br /></strong>We’re on a mission to open the world to everyone, giving our customers unlimited choice, unmatched ease and unmissable value for their next getaway.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our <strong>trailblaze together</strong> culture is what drives our success, powered by our people and the way they work. Using progressive technology, we <strong>drive cutting-edge innovation</strong> and improve how our customers discover, book and experience their holidays. You’ll have the opportunity to <strong>accelerate your growth</strong> through meaningful challenges, new experiences and the freedom to shape your own path. <strong>You’ll create impact for our future</strong> by taking ownership, contributing to shared goals and helping shape what comes next, all as part of our <strong>enhanced international community</strong> of talented, collaborative and passionate teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The difference you’ll make</strong><br /><br />You'll sit in the Aviation team, reporting to the Senior Operations Manager. You'll work closely with Commercial, Supply Tech, Product and Finance to own ticketing and disruption performance across our 140+ airline partners, making sure every flight we sell is ticketed correctly and every schedule change is handled quickly, accurately and fairly. Together, the team uses airline know-how, data and automation to protect revenue, reduce manual effort and give customers a consistent experience whenever their travel plans change, in every market we sell in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aviation sits within our Enablement function, where everything we do starts with the customer. From the moment someone books to the day they arrive home, Customer Experience teams make sure they feel looked after, especially when things don't go to plan. By turning what we learn from every booking, contact and disruption into better processes, clearer communication and smarter tools, the Customer function helps build the trust that brings customers back to loveholidays time and again.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your day-to-day:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own ticketing and amendment quality including both managed and self-managed airline relationships, keeping queues clear and disruption handled consistently</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the day-to-day operational performance of the team, maintaining strong operational grip across queue health, ticketing turnaround, SLA adherence and quality. Use data and insight to identify recurring issues, drive continuous improvement and translate findings into clear, actionable recommendations that improve performance and customer outcomes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the team's subject matter expert for Amadeus Robotics, driving adoption of automation and robotic tools across the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share best practice from the core market across all points of sale, keeping process documentation current and consistently applied.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Play a central role in getting Flight Ticketing &amp; Disruption ready for new market launches, from process setup to team readiness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, coach and motivate a team of ticketing agent