ering support through a globally distributed follow-the-sun support model, ensuring timely incident response and resolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor and improve system health, availability, performance, and reliability through observability, alerting, and proactive operational practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independently troubleshoot production incidents, perform root cause analysis (RCA), and implement preventive measures to reduce recurring issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain automation solutions to reduce manual intervention, improve operational efficiency, and minimize human error.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, maintain, and improve CI/CD pipelines to enable reliable, secure, and efficient software deployments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage cloud infrastructure using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools such as Terraform, ensuring consistency, scalability, and repeatability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support and optimize containerized workloads and orchestration platforms, including Kubernetes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and address reliability risks, performance bottlenecks, and infrastructure scalability challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to incident management processes, post-incident reviews, operational runbooks, and continuous improvement initiatives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Software Engineering, DevOps, QE, Security, and Product teams to ensure production readiness and reliable product delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive improvements in operational excellence through automation, monitoring enhancements, and adoption of SRE best practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in technical discussions, architecture reviews, and production readiness assessments to ensure systems meet operational and reliability requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share technical knowledge, contribute to engineering standards, and support the development of junior team members.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with SRE team members and Engineering organizations based in California, Paris, Nantong, Singapore, Australia, and other global locations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Required Skills:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3–5 years of hands-on experience in Site Reliability Engineering, DevOps, Production Engineering, Cloud Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of Linux systems, networking fundamentals, and production infrastructure operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with public cloud platforms such as AWS, GCP, or Azure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience deploying, managing, and troubleshooting containerized applications using Kubernetes and Docker.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and maintaining CI/CD pipelines using tools such as Jenkins, GitHub Actions, or ArgoCD.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency with Infrastructure as Code tools such as Terraform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong scripting or programming skills in Python, Bash, Go, or similar languages, with the ability to develop operational automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with monitoring, logging, and observability tools such as Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog, or similar platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of incident management, troubleshooting methodologies, root cause analysis, and production support practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with distributed systems, high availability, scalability, and reliability engineering principles.</p></li><li>