mpany_name":"Chainalysis","title":"Technical Recruiter, EMEA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">The R&amp;D team at Chainalysis is inspired by solving the hardest challenges and building products that establish trust in cryptocurrencies. We're a global organization that thrives on challenging work and doing it alongside exceptionally talented teammates. Our industry evolves rapidly, and our mission is to build a flexible, AI-driven platform that automates entity resolution, optimizes data labeling pipelines, and creates predictive models that identify illicit patterns before they escalate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our data and solutions have been used to solve some of the world's most high-profile criminal cases and grow consumer access to cryptocurrency safely. Now, by pairing the industry's most trusted blockchain data with agents that reason, investigate, and act, we help our customers scale their workflows as the cryptocurrency economy becomes increasingly mainstream.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talent Acquisition at Chainalysis is a small, close-knit team that partners with leaders across the business to hire the people who will carry our mission forward. We share sourcing wins, market learnings, and process improvements openly, and we hold ourselves to a high bar for both results and candidate experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are hiring a Technical Recruiter to own and drive hiring for Engineering &amp; Product roles in our EMEA locations. This is a high-volume, outbound-heavy role: you'll spend a meaningful portion of your time building pipeline through direct sourcing, identifying and engaging top engineering talent across AI, Crypto, and Fintech. You'll manage a full requisition load, move fast, and close strong candidates in a competitive market, with Software Engineering roles among your key hires. You'll work closely with hiring managers across our R&amp;D teams as a talent partner who understands the business and delivers results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>In this role, you'll:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build pipeline through proactive outbound sourcing, mapping the AI, crypto, and fintech landscape to find where strong Software Engineers work today</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop creative sourcing strategies that go beyond LinkedIn InMails, including referral generation, community engagement, and direct outreach campaigns</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full recruiting lifecycle for R&amp;D roles, from intake and sourcing through offer negotiation and close, across a high-volume requisition load</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver a thoughtful, personalised, and transparent candidate experience at every step while moving candidates through the process efficiently</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with R&amp;D leaders to calibrate expectations, share market insights on talent availability and compensation, and flag risks early so hiring plans stay on schedule</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use data on pipeline health, conversion rates, and channel effectiveness to guide decisions, and champion diversity and inclusion in every search</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>We're looking for candidates who have:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience with a strong track record of hiring technical talent, such as Software Engineers, Data Scientists, Researchers, and Product Managers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated outbound sourcing ability: you build your own pipeline through direct outreach and do not rely on inbound applications to fill roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High AI proficiency, using it for building pipeline proactively, workflows, processes, and documentation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience recruiting technical talent within the SaaS, AI, Blockchain, and Cybersecurity sectors, with a focus on candidates who have worked in fast-paced companies building technically complex products</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consistently utilised data to inform decision making and advise hiring managers through the hiring process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisational skills, sharp attention to detail, and consistent follow-through on every candidate and requisition</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to build credibility with hiring managers quickly, communicate market realities clearly, and guide decisions with data, in a collaborative, low-ego way</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>You might also have:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience recruiting for Blockchain companies with a focus on Engineering roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A background at a high-growth scale up technology company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of hiring for technical roles in Denmark, Israel, UK, and the USA</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Tools we use:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ashby ATS</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sourcing tools (LinkedIn Recruiter, Nova AI, GitHub)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coderpad</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Google suite, Slack, Chain AI</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Chainalysis</strong><br />AI is not a feature at Chainalysis - it is a new way of working. One that turns instructions into work done, and helps us move faster than the threats we're built to counter, and we expect our employees to take ownership of the output and ensure quality. As the world's most trusted blockchain analytics platform, Chainalysis sits at a rare intersection of proprietary data, regulatory relationships and crypto expertise that makes it uniquely placed to shape and lead the next era of AI-driven intelligence - and we expect everyone here, regardless of role, to be an active part of it.<br /><br />AI fluency is tied directly to how we measure performance and how we plan to win. There is no substitute for your own curiosity. We provide the tools, workflows, and space to experiment - but the expectation is that you develop these capabilities yourself, bring ideas, and collaborate across teams to reinvent the way work gets done. We are not using AI to do less. We are using it to do what was never possible before.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Chainalysis</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Chainalysis is the blockchain data platform, making it easy to connect the movement of digital assets to real-world services. Powered by deep blockchain data and AI, organizations can investigate illicit activity, manage risk exposure, and develop innovative market solutions built on the industry's most trusted blockchain intelligence. Our mission is to build trust in blockchains, blending safety and security with an unwavering commitment to growth and innovation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You belong here. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Chainalysis, we believe that diversity of experience and thought makes us stronger. With both customers and employees around the world, we are committed to ensuring our team reflects the unique communities around us. We’re ensuring we keep learning by committing to continually revisit and reevaluate our diversity culture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We encourage applicants across any race, ethnicity, gender/gender expression, age, spirituality, ability, experience and more. If you need any accommodations to make our interview process more accessible to you due to a disability, don't hesitate to let us know. You can learn more <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://go.chainalysis.com/rs/503-FAP-074/images/Interview%20Accommodations%20Request.pdf">here</a>. We can’t wait to meet you. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/chainalysis/technical-recruiter-emea-united-kingdom-431591","tags":["Corporate Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1793947210},{"slug":"sr-product-marketing-manager-government-london-4141","company_name":"Chainalysis","title":"Sr. Product Marketing Manager, Government","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Product Marketing turns Chainalysis innovation into customer value. We position our intelligence as solutions customers can understand and consume through our platform, shape how we commercialize them, and give GTM the stories and strategic assets to win.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The public sector is a priority growth segment for Chainalysis, spanning law enforcement, intelligence agencies, regulators and tax authorities. As digital assets become more integrated into the financial system, these organizations need the intelligence, tools and tradecraft to advance their missions—from shaping policy and enforcing the rules to disrupting illicit networks and protecting national security. This role connects Chainalysis capabilities to those mission priorities, with a clear, compelling story for agency leaders and operational teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Senior Product Marketing Manager for the Public Sector, you will own how Chainalysis shows up in the market for these buyers. You will shape our intelligence, data, products, AI capabilities, and services into a differentiated customer story—one that connects to real workflows, urgent problems, and mission outcomes.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role for a strong marketer and an exceptional writer. You can take a complex capability, a shifting market, or a fuzzy customer problem and shape it into a sharp point of view, a persuasive narrative, and practical tools that sellers and customers actually use. You will work closely with Product, Sales, Marketing &amp; Communications, subject-matter experts, and GTM Solutions &amp; Readiness teams to make the story land in the market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In this role, you’ll:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Position the value</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and evolve the public sector value narrative: what Chainalysis enables, why it matters, and why we are meaningfully different.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build messaging for priority buyer and user personas, from agency leaders to investigators, intelligence analysts, regulators and tax specialists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create the narratives, proof points, and strategic assets that help sellers communicate differentiated value with conviction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own public-sector competitive intelligence, translating market moves into clear offensive and defensive positioning for deal teams.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn value into solutions</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product, R&amp;D, Marketing &amp; Communications, and subject-matter experts to translate innovation into compelling industry solutions, use cases, and sales plays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead go-to-market planning for launches, major releases, platform capabilities, and commercial offerings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape customer-facing value narratives for pricing, packaging, and usage-based commercial models, including business cases, operational value and mission impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring a customer lens to product and market decisions: explain not only what a capability does, but how it advances the customer’s mission.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Win and learn in market</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce the strategic content that moves government opportunities forward: first-call decks, solution briefs, talk tracks, discovery frameworks, proof points, and sales plays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product, Product Marketing, GTM &amp; Enablement teams to scale the strongest narratives into field tools and enablement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring customer, field, partner, and competitive insight back into the work — sharpening positioning, converting market evidence into credible stories, and building repeatable use cases.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’re looking for candidates who have: <br /></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5–8 years in product, solutions, industry, or B2B enterprise technology marketing, with experience marketing to public-sector customers across law enforcement, intelligence, regulatory or tax functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A demonstrated ability to build positioning and messaging that changes how customers and sellers see a problem—not simply content that fills a library.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional writing and editorial judgment. You can write crisp headlines, persuasive narratives, practical sales content, and executive-level messaging; you know the difference between jargon and precision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of public-sector buying journeys, decision-making processes and mission-oriented sales motions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to connect technical capabilities to mission and operational value for both executive buyers and hands-on users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative self-starter, comfortable working across R&amp;D, Sales, technical and revenue teams, and senior leaders to drive ambiguous, multi-stakeholder work forward independently.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have experience:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with blockchain, digital assets, or crypto-native financial infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience marketing AI-powered products, data platforms, intelligence products, cybersecurity, or risk and compliance technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with consumption- or usage-based pricing and packaging.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with investigative, intelligence, national-security, regulatory or tax use cases for intelligence and technology, and the policy developments shaping digital-asset markets.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’ll thrive here if:</strong><br /><br />You can shape complexity into a story people remember and a sales conversation people can use. You write with precision, bring sound judgment to ambiguous problems, build for repeatability rather than one-off requests, and care about the quality of what reaches customers and the field.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Chainalysis</strong><br />AI is not a feature at Chainalysis - it is a new way of working. One that turns instructions into work done, and helps us move faster than the threats we're built to counter, and we expect our employees to take ownership of the output and ensure quality. As the world's most trusted blockchain analytics