 exposure, and develop innovative market solutions built on the industry's most trusted blockchain intelligence. Our mission is to build trust in blockchains, blending safety and security with an unwavering commitment to growth and innovation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You belong here. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Chainalysis, we believe that diversity of experience and thought makes us stronger. With both customers and employees around the world, we are committed to ensuring our team reflects the unique communities around us. We’re ensuring we keep learning by committing to continually revisit and reevaluate our diversity culture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We encourage applicants across any race, ethnicity, gender/gender expression, age, spirituality, ability, experience and more. If you need any accommodations to make our interview process more accessible to you due to a disability, don't hesitate to let us know. You can learn more <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://go.chainalysis.com/rs/503-FAP-074/images/Interview%20Accommodations%20Request.pdf">here</a>. We can’t wait to meet you. </p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/chainalysis/senior-software-engineer-aggregation-search-united-kingdom-371637","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1793947210},{"slug":"senior-frontend-engineer-marketing-website-london-337459","company_name":"Synthesia","title":"Senior Frontend Engineer, Marketing Website","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Synthesia is the world’s leading AI video platform for business, used by over 90% of the Fortune 100. Founded in 2017, the company is headquartered in London, with offices and teams across Europe and the US. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As AI continues to shape the way we live and work, Synthesia develops products to enhance visual communication and enterprise skill development, helping people work better and stay at the center of successful organizations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Following our recent Series E funding round, where we raised $200 million, our valuation stands at $4 billion. Our total funding exceeds $530 million from premier investors including Accel, NVentures (Nvidia's VC arm), Kleiner Perkins, GV, and Evantic Capital, alongside the founders and operators of Stripe, Datadog, Miro, and Webflow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Frontend Engineer on our Website team, you'll be a co-owner of the platform behind <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://synthesia.io">synthesia.io</a>: the component library, content model and rendering stack that every page on our marketing site is built from. You'll shape direction and make key technical decisions with the team, likely with a focus area of your own but context across the whole system. This is a hands-on engineering role, and your primary output is high-quality component and schema code, plus the tooling that lets others build with it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Millions of people visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://synthesia.io">synthesia.io</a> every month, and it is one of the main ways we win new customers. That comes with real responsibility. The decisions you make are seen at scale, and we set the quality bar accordingly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The defining challenge of this role is composability: a marketing site that marketers, and increasingly AI agents, can build pages with, without breaking design, performance or SEO.<br /></p><h3><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, scale and evolve our section library: the Astro components, Sanity schemas and design tokens that let us compose marketing pages consistently and accessibly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the content model. Design schemas that resist misuse, so an editor, or an agent, can build a page that is correct by construction rather than correct by review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take Figma component specs all the way to production: responsive across mobile, tablet and desktop, accessible by default, matching design intent precisely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extend the platform for AI-assisted development, so coding agents can generate on-brand, on-spec sections from a design spec as reliably as a person can.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own SEO integrity as a first-class engineering concern: canonicals, sitemaps, structured data, redirects, and no traffic cliffs on launch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Raise the bar on engineering standards across the website surface: thorough code review, patterns others can follow, and tests around the parts that actually break.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain and extend localisation across nine locales and a translation pipeline, so the system works for a global audience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape the technical direction of the website platform over the next 6 to 12 months, and champion its adoption with the people who publish on it.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>We’d love to hear from you if you have</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least five (5+) years as a software engineer, including three (3) at senior level, building front end for content-driven or marketing platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real ownership of a content model in Sanity.</strong> You've designed schemas other people had to live with, and you have opinions about references vs. embedded objects, when a variant belongs in the schema versus at runtime, and how to stop a section library sprawling. GROQ and Portable Text are familiar territory.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep front-end expertise: expert HTML, CSS and TypeScript, with a strong command of component API design and the developer experience of a shared library.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You can work end to end.</strong> Comfortable owning the server side as well as the front end: SSR, serverless and edge runtimes, API routes, a SQL database, secrets and CI. You should be able to take a feature from schema to component to the route that serves it without handing off, and be happy debugging something that only reproduces in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of responsive design, cross-browser compatibility and web performance, and comfortable building to WCAG 2.2 AA. Accessibility is part of your definition of done, not a separate pass.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care that marketing sites are measured, on performance, SEO, analytics events and conversion, and you're happy being accountable to those numbers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong sense of craft and attention to detail, and the judgement to balance design intent against engineering constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication and collaboration skills. You explain your reasoning, review generously, and treat levelling up the people around you as part of the job.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>We’d be particularly excited if</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior experience working on a large SaaS marketing website, at real traffic and with real stakes attached.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Astro, or another islands or static-site framework.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cloudflare Workers, or another edge or serverless platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with AWS Lambda.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tailwind CSS v4, and experience working from a token-based design system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience, or strong interest, in making component libraries and content models consumable by AI agents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong design sensibility: an eye for visual detail and the judgement to push back on and improve design decisions, not just build them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with localisation and internationalisation at scale for a global audience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytics and tag management implementation: dataLayer events, server-side tagging, getting attribution right without hurting performance.<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location</strong><br />Our preference is for this role to be based hybrid out of our London, UK office. We can also accommodate remote workers elsewhere in Europe subject to compliance and right to work checks.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/synthesia/senior-frontend-engineer-marketing-website-london-337459","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793947210},{"slug":"senior-lifecycle-manager-london-10734","company_name":"Synthesia","title":"Senior Lifecycle Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Synthesia is the world’s leading AI video platform for business, used by over 90% of the Fortune 100. Founded in 2017, the company is headquartered in London, with offices and teams across Europe and the US. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As AI continues to shape the way we live and work, Synthesia develops products to enhance visual communication and enterprise skill development, helping people work better and stay at the center of successful organizations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Following our recent Series E funding round, where we raised $200 million, our valuation stands at $4 billion. Our total funding exceeds $530 million from premier investors including Accel, NVentures (Nvidia's VC arm), Kleiner Perkins, GV, and Evantic Capital, alongside the founders and operators of Stripe, Datadog, Miro, and Webflow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Synthesia is growing fast, and lifecycle is how we turn that growth into lasting customer relationships, guiding every user from first signup to real value. Every month we send 150+ emails to 1+ million contacts, and as we launch new products and enter new markets, that scale and its impact on revenue will keep rising.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Senior Lifecycle Manager, you’ll build one of the most exciting lifecycle programmes in Europe. You’ll own the product-led growth motion after signup: the journeys that turn new users into activated, paying and expanding customers. You’ll build automations triggered by what users do in the product and set the standard for how every customer-facing email Synthesia sends works together as one experience. You’ll partner with Product, Product Marketing and Data teams to build a lifecycle engine that grows with the company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer journeys:</strong> Design, build and optimise lifecycle journeys that support customers throughout their experience with Synthesia, from activation, adoption and engagement through to expansion, retention and winback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lifecycle automation:</strong> Own the end-to-end implementation of lifecycle programmes, from audience segmentation and behavioural triggers to workflow logic, suppression rules, QA and performance monitoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experimentation: </strong>Develop and execute structured experiments to continuously improve lifecycle performance. Test messaging, timing, segmentation and journey design, analyse results and turn learnings into actionable improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data-driven personalisation: </strong>Leverage product usage, customer attributes and engagement signals to deliver increasingly relevant lifecycle experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lifecycle quality and deliverability:</strong> Own campaign QA and testing processes, support email deliverability and sender reputation and help establish best practices for segmentation, frequency management and customer experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-powered lifecycle: </strong>Explore and apply AI to make lifecycle marketing more effective and efficient. From content creation and dynamic personalisation to workflow automation, identify opportunities to improve both the customer experience and how we work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>We’d love to hear from you if you have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You deliver impact: </strong>You understand how lifecycle marketing contributes to activation, adoption, retention and revenue, and you can demonstrate measurable results from programmes you’ve owned</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’re analytical and curious:</strong> You use data to understand performance, challenge assumptions and continuously improve what you build</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You think in customer journeys:</strong> You look beyond individual emails to understand the customer experience, identify friction and create relevant, connected communications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’re technically excellent:</strong> You’re confident building sophisticated automation, managing complex segmentation and working with customer and product data. You care about the details that make programmes effective and reliable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You take ownership:</strong> You’re comfortable independently leading initiatives from concept through execution, proactively solving problems and making informed decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You collaborate naturally:</strong> You know how to work across functions, build strong relationships and move complex projects forward without direct authority</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You care about quality:</strong> From deliverability and data accuracy to messaging and customer experience, you hold your work to a high standard</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’re excited about AI:</strong> You actively explore how emerging technologies can improve personalisation, experimentation and the way lifecycle marketing operates</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>We’d be particularly excited if</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ years of experience in lifecycle, CRM or email marketing, ideally in B2B SaaS or product-led companies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong hands-on experience with HubSpot, including complex workflows, list building, segmentation and campaign execution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience building and optimising always-on automated programmes, including onboarding, nurture and re-engagement, alongside one-off campaigns</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience owning lifecycle initiatives end to end, from briefing and journey design to implementation, QA, reporting and optimisation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills, with experience using product, CRM and engagement data to build audiences, evaluate performance and run structured experiments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5e