with customers and help shape what we build. Sometimes you'll spot the next problem yourself, and sometimes we'll hand you a clear priority to run with.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Spend real time with customers.</strong> Join calls and site visits, sit with the people who do the work, and understand why they do it the way they do. You'll know their problems firsthand, not from a ticket.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape what to build.</strong> Turn what you hear into a clear problem, a scope and a plan, and push back when the obvious request isn't the real need. When we bring you a priority, you'll own how it gets solved.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build it.</strong> Design and build backend services in Go and Python that turn messy tenders, catalogs and purchase orders into data customers can rely on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ship, then check.</strong> Get it in front of customers fast, watch how they actually use it, and iterate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own it in production.</strong> When something breaks at a customer, it's yours to understand and fix.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build with AI.</strong> Use AI heavily in how you work, and design systems that agents can use as well as people.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What success looks like after 3 months</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">There's a part of the product people now think of as yours, and you're the one deciding what happens to it next</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've spotted a problem nobody asked you to solve, made the case for it, and shipped a first version</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've shipped features from both sources: priorities we set and ideas from your own customer conversations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least once, you've talked us out of building something customers didn't really need</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've left a part of the platform simpler than you found it</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>You'll probably thrive here if</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've taken something from zero to one: a company, a product line, or a side project with paying users</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built and run backend systems in production that other people depend on. We care more about your judgment than your language; you're strong in Go or Python and happy to work in both</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're solid on data modeling, API design and messy real-world data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather talk to a customer than wait for a spec</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable with ambiguity. You can make progress while the problem is still half-defined, which at a startup it usually is</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want a large scope of responsibility and are happy to own things well beyond your job title</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rapidly changing requirements don't throw you. When customers or priorities shift, you adapt and keep going</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy direct customer contact and want to be on customer calls</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You make things simpler over time, not more clever</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write clearly in English. German is a plus, not a requirement</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>You probably won't enjoy it if</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You just want to code and go home</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't like talking to customers, whether on calls or on the occasional site visit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ambiguity and chaos bother you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want a well-defined backlog handed to you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your main goal is managing people soon. Here, scope grows with what you own, not with headcount</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Our stack</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Go and Python (FastAPI), PostgreSQL, GCP, and LLMs throughout the document pipeline. You don't need to know all of it on day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we hire</h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Screening call (30 min)</strong> with our VP Engineering. It's two-way: ask us anything, including the hard questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical deep-dive call</strong>: walk us through something you built from scratch, the decisions you made and what went wrong.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet Scalera Day</strong>: join us remotely to work on a real problem with real (anonymized) construction documents, and meet the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer</strong>: if it's a fit on both sides, we'll move quickly to an offer.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Working at Scalera</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote within the EU or EEA</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Small team, no bureaucracy. You'll work directly with the CEO, CTO, VP Engineering and Customer Success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Founders and former founders:</strong> if you're unsure whether you fit, send a few lines about what you built and why you moved on. We read every one.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/scalera/senior-backend-ai-engineer-remote-zurich-344461","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["