&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/auterion/forward-deployed-engineer-amsterdam-20835","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793883319},{"slug":"nanofabrication-technician-delft-168721","company_name":"Quantware","title":"Nanofabrication Technician","description":"<h2><strong>About Us </strong><br /></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">QuantWare is building the world’s most powerful quantum processors to solve humanity's greatest challenges. We do this with our unique VIO™ technology, the only QPU architecture that breaks the hardware barriers that have held quantum computing back, unlocking the path to MegaQubit quantum processors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With VIO, we are paving the way for the hyper-scale quantum computers that will change the world. And delivering on that vision demands people who don’t shy away from tackling the hardest challenges of our time. That’s where you come in! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tool Operation &amp; Processing:</strong> Safely and accurately operate cleanroom production equipment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process Execution:</strong> Strictly follow established recipes, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), and safety guidelines to ensure consistent wafer-scale fabrication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Quality &amp; Monitoring:</strong> Monitor tool performance during production runs. Perform basic inspections of the wafers and immediately flag any anomalies, defects, or machine errors to the engineering team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accurate Documentation:</strong> Log production data, batch records, and tool usage clearly and accurately to maintain full traceability of our products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cleanroom Maintenance:</strong> Help maintain a pristine working environment, ensuring workstations are prepped, materials are stocked, and cleanroom protocols are strictly followed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring practical experience from a high-precision manufacturing environment and possess the discipline to work independently in an academic cleanroom environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills, able to collaborate effectively across R&amp;D and production teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organized &amp; detail-oriented, able to document your work clearly and follow established procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a clear communicator who works well in a team and knows when to escalate issues to the engineers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don't tick every box? Apply anyway! Research shows women often self-select out if they don't meet every requirement. Here's our take: nobody ticks every box. This is a description of our ideal candidate, not a filter. If most resonates and you're keen to learn the gaps, apply. We hire for trajectory, not perfection. <br /><br /><strong>What We Offer:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At QuantWare, you’ll be part of a high-performing team of world-class experts in an ambitious, fast-moving environment. From day one, you’ll have the trust, tools, and support to do your best work. Here’s what you can expect:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive salary</strong> - A salary that reflects the impact and importance of the role (and of course 8% holiday allowance)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension that’s built to last</strong> - A generous and future-proof pension plan that includes partner and dependent coverage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility built on trust</strong> - We focus on outcomes. Work flexibly, in a hybrid setup, with an open vacation policy that lets you manage your time</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal growth</strong> - We invest in your L&amp;D, with a budget available to each team member, dependent on their individual ambitions, development needs, and performance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A connected team</strong> - We make space to celebrate wins together, with team events, offsites, and spontaneous moments that bring us closer<br /><br /><strong>Diversity &amp; Inclusion at QuantWare</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re an ambitious company, not only for our goals but also to become an even more diverse and inclusive team. We know great candidates don't always follow a straight path, and we value diverse experience, perspectives, and ways of thinking. We know this helps us make better decisions, drives more innovation, and strengthens our culture. <br /><br /><em>As part of our recruitment process, candidates may be required to undergo pre-employment screening.</em></p><h2></h2><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/quantware/nanofabrication-technician-delft-168721","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Delft","created_at":1793882432},{"slug":"customer-service-agent-amsterdam-192371","company_name":"Crisp","title":"Customer Service Agent","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Bij Crisp staan onze klanten op nummer één. Ons gezellige en hechte serviceteam doet er alles aan om die klanten van de beste service te voorzien. We hebben daarom veel persoonlijk contact met de klant, en ondersteunen onze bezorgers voor een vlekkeloze bezorging. We zijn nog volop in ontwikkeling, dus je denkt ook mee over hoe we onze service kunnen verbeteren.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Wat je gaat doen</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je hebt elke dag direct contact met onze klanten, vooral via Whatsapp. Zo maak je ze nog blijer nadat ze ons gesproken hebben. Daarnaast geef je feedback van klanten door aan de juiste teams binnen Crisp, zodat we onze service kunnen blijven verbeteren. Ook zorg je samen met onze bezorgers en je collega's op onze logistieke hubs dat bezorgingen vlekkeloos verlopen. Verder verdiep je je in onze processen. Zoals je al hoort, geen dag is hetzelfde!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hoe ziet een werkdag eruit?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">'s Ochtends hou je onze bezorgroutes goed in de gaten. Is het druk op de weg? Dan zorg jij ervoor dat onze klanten op tijd weten dat hun bezorger iets later is.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ondertussen pak je WhatsApp-berichtjes van klanten op. Je helpt ze met het aanpassen van hun bestelling, het kiezen van een bezorgtijd of beantwoordt vragen over ons assortiment. Zo leer je elke dag iets nieuws over eten!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunchtijd! Elke dag lunchen we met onze eigen boodschappen. Een ideaal moment om ons assortiment én je collega's beter te leren kennen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Na de lunch beantwoord je vragen via WhatsApp, social media en e-mail, terwijl je collega's de bezorgingen in de gaten houden of bezig zijn met de processen. Je merkt dat er veel vragen zijn over een bepaalde marketingactie. Dat geef je dus meteen even door aan de juiste collega.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">De collega's die 's avonds werken nemen jouw taken over. Dat zorgt ervoor dat je de feedback die klanten doorgeven via de app nog even kunt verwerken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tijd om af te sluiten. Samen met je collega's drink je nog een ijskoud Crisp-drankje in onze gezellige keuken.</p></li></ul><h1>Dit ben jij</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je herkent je in het volgende profiel:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent parttime (16-24 uur per week) beschikbaar. We zijn 7 dagen per week open van 07:30 tot 23:00 uur, en je werkt straks in shifts van 4 tot 8 uur. Daarom is flexibele beschikbaarheid voor overdag, avonden én in het weekend een must.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je woont in omgeving Amsterdam en bent voor minimaal één jaar beschikbaar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een kantoor in de Amsterdamse Pijp met een grote keuken waar flink wordt geluncht, gezellig gekookt en waar de kans op zelfgebakken taart of vegan roze koeken groot is. <strong>Goed om te weten: vanaf januari 2027 groeien we door en verhuizen we naar een gloednieuwe, grotere locatie in de buurt van Zaandam, Sloterdijk en de Houthavens, waar we vanaf dan onze nieuwe thuisbasis hebben.</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je schrijft en spreekt vloeiend Nederlands. Op een persoonlijke en creatieve manier reageren op klanten gaat jou makkelijk af.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent oplossingsgericht en empathisch. Je kunt je verplaatsen in onze klanten en begrijpt wat er nodig is om hun ervaring met Crisp nog beter te maken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bedenkt creatieve oplossingen om onze klanten te verrassen en verwachtingen te overtreffen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als je klantenservice-ervaring hebt binnen organisaties waar kwaliteit hoog in het vaandel staat, is dat super!</p></li></ul><h1>Wat wij bieden</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een marktconform salaris, afhankelijk van leeftijd.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een gezellig en hecht team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Veel verantwoordelijkheid, uitdagend werk en een dynamische omgeving.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een kijkje in de keuken van een snelgroeiende start-up. We zijn volop in ontwikkeling dus jouw ideeën tellen mee.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Werken bij een B-Corp gecertificeerd bedrijf, waarbij je de kans krijgt om je stempel te drukken op ons voedselsysteem en échte verandering teweeg te brengen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enthousiaste en ondernemende collega’s om mee te werken en te leren.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Voor straks een perfect pensioen via BPFL.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Voor nu een persoonlijk budget voor yoga, sport, mobiliteit en downtime via bijvoorbeeld ClassPass, Pathé en Blendle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Elke maand food for thought, met workshops en talks via de Crisp University.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tijd om je collega’s te leren kennen tijdens sport, events en proeverijen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een kantoor in de Amsterdamse Pijp met een grote keuken waar flink wordt geluncht, gezellig gekookt en grote kans op zelfgebakken taart of vegan roze koeken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">En... fikse korting op je Crisp boodschappen, omdat je thuis natuurlijk ook goed wilt eten.</p></li></ul><h1>Ben jij geïnteresseerd?</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Is de functie van Service Agent jou op het lijf geschreven, solliciteer dan via onderstaand button. Hoe meer je kunt delen over jezelf en de reden dat je solliciteert, hoe beter.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bij Crisp streven we naar een inclusieve en diverse werkomgeving waarin iedereen welkom is, ongeacht hun achtergrond, geslacht, leeftijd, etniciteit, seksuele geaardheid, religie of beperking. Wij moedigen sollicitanten met diverse perspectieven en achtergronden aan om te solliciteren en geloven in gelijke kansen voor iedereen. We waarderen de unieke bijdragen die elke medewerker kan leveren en zijn vastbesloten om een inclusieve werkplek te creëren waarin iedereen wordt gerespecteerd en gewaardeerd.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/crisp/customer-service-agent-amsterdam-192371","tags":["Customer Experience"],"job_types":["Part Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793882432},{"slug":"enterprise-applications-manager-amsterdam-195948","company_name":"Skynrg","title":"Enterprise Applications Manager","description":"<h1><strong>Enterprise Applications Manager</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About the role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As SkyNRG grows, applications such as SAP Public Cloud, HubSpot, and our Inventory Management System are becoming increasingly important to our operations. We are looking for an Enterprise Applications Manager to take functional ownership of this landscape and ensure our systems effectively support the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will connect business needs with IT solutions, translating requests into clear requirements and coordinated improvements. Working across Commercial, Operations, Maintenance, HSE, Finance and QA, you will create structure, improve adoption and act as the main point of contact for our enterprise applications.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your key responsibilities include:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take functional ownership of SAP Public Cloud, including EAM and HSE, HubSpot, IMS, and other enterprise applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate business processes and needs into clear requirements, functional designs, user stories and test scenarios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage functional support, incidents and change requests, coordinating with external partners and vendors where necessary.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain the enterprise application roadmap, backlogs and change priorities with IT and business owners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Configure applications within the functional scope and coordinate releases, testing and implementation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve application adoption, data quality, reporting and integrations across the application landscape.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain process documentation, user guides, application records and access roles in line with security and compliance requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Train and support key users across the organization, helping teams make effective use of the available systems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your initial focus will include strengthening the use of SAP EAM and HSE, improving HubSpot’s commercial processes and reporting, and introducing a consistent intake and change process for business requests.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">While this role does not have direct reports, you will coordinate external implementation partners and application vendors. You will also work closely with the wider IT team to ensure our enterprise applications are reliable, secure and aligned with business priorities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a growing company in a rapidly evolving industry, we are looking for people who embrace change and are motivated to actively contribute to building and scaling our business. You feel comfortable in an entrepreneurial environment, take ownership, and thrive when things are still developing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand both business processes and enterprise technology. You can move comfortably between conversations with business stakeholders, technical colleagues, and external partners, translating different perspectives into practical solutions. Structured and pragmatic, you take end-to-end responsibility rather than simply passing requests along.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You recognize yourself in the following:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bachelor’s or master’s degree in Business Administration, Information Management, Industrial Engineering, or a related discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least five years of experience as a Business Analyst, Functional Consultant, Application Owner, or in a comparable enterprise applications role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on functional experience with SAP, ideally SAP S/4HANA Public Cloud, in at least one relevant area such as EAM or Plant Maintenance, HSE or EHS, Finance, or Procurement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with a CRM platform, preferably HubSpot.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to translate business processes and needs into clear requirements, functional designs, and test scenarios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing application vendors or implementation partners, including support agreements and service levels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of change management, release management, testing and access control in an enterprise environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder-management and communication skills, with the ability to constructively challenge business requests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional fluency in English.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in an industrial, energy, chemical, manufacturing or asset-intensive environment would be an advantage. Familiarity with system integrations, SAP BTP, APIs, Power BI or data-quality initiatives would also be beneficial. Knowledge of relevant regulatory and compliance frameworks, such as NIS2, ISO 27001 and GDPR, is considered a plus.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About SkyNRG</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2009, SkyNRG has been a change maker in the aviation industry. We are dedicated to supplying and producing high-integrity Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), making sustainable aviation a reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaboration is fundamental to achieving our ambition. We nurture genuine relationships with global partners in our drive to make SAF <em>the</em> alternative to fossil jet fuel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our in-house team of SAF experts have helped over 60 airlines and corporates reduce their climate impact using the Book &amp; Claim mechanism; the most transparent and traceable way to support aviation sustainability with real emission reductions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sustainability is woven into the fabric of our company. We maintain an independent Sustainability Board, which advises the company on feedstocks and provides strategic guidance on wide-ranging sustainability issues. SkyNRG operations are certified against the RSB EU RED, CORSIA, and Book &amp; Claim standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At SkyNRG, you’ll find:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An innovation-driven culture – where big ideas turn into real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth opportunities – in a fast-scaling, industry-changing company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative team – where your ideas and expertise are valued</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A mission that matters – leading the change in the energy transition by producing and supplying high-integrity SAF</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What we offer</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a brand-new office in the heart of Amsterdam, designed for collaboration and creativity. Most importantly, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to a truly game-changing green initiative, making a real impact on the aviation industry and the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Besides that, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">30 paid holidays + 2 for choosing sustainable travel options for your holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to a sustainable organization (B Corp)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attractive bonus scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">€5.000,- dedicated budget every 3 years for professional development</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commuting travel reimbursement + Lease a Bike plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An office in the city centre of Amsterdam (Nieuwmarkt)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work where it feels best for you: we offer flexible (hybrid in-office) working arrangements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous employer pension contribution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid Volunteering Day</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to our electric company boat (also available for private use), free lunch, and lots of social activities – all part of the deal!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Is this you?</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to take the next step in your career with SkyNRG? Explore our vacancies and become part of our company of change makers. Together, we can change the future of flying.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information about SkyNRG visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.skynrg.com"><u>www.skynrg.com</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>📌 Please note: We do not accept sales inquiries or intermediary services.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At SkyNRG, we deeply value inclusion and diversity. As an equal opportunity employer, we are dedicated to ensuring every applicant has a fair chance, irrespective of race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, or any other legally protected characteristics.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skynrg/enterprise-applications-manager-amsterdam-195948","tags":["IT"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793882432},{"slug":"chief-investment-officer-cio-amsterdam-215904","company_name":"Skynrg","title":"Chief Investment Officer (CIO)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">As one of the leading companies in Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), SkyNRG is developing and advancing projects, partnerships and commercial opportunities that will play a critical role in the decarbonization of aviation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our portfolio grows in scale and complexity, we are looking to further strengthen our investment capabilities, combining strategic thinking, commercial insight and disciplined decision-making to accelerate value creation across the business. To support this next stage of growth, we are seeking a Chief Investment Officer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting directly to the CEO and working closely with the Executive Committee, Board and shareholders, the CIO will play a central role in shaping the future direction of SkyNRG. This executive will bring an institutional investor mindset to the organization, strengthening how opportunities are evaluated, prioritized and executed while ensuring that capital is deployed toward initiatives that create sustainable strategic and financial value.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Chief Investment Officer will be responsible for leading SkyNRG's Investment Management capability and driving value creation across the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with the Executive Committee, Board and shareholders, the CIO will help shape the strategic direction of SkyNRG by ensuring investment decisions, capital allocation and growth initiatives are aligned with long-term value creation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role combines the analytical rigor of an investment professional with the strategic perspective of a business leader. It offers the opportunity to influence some of the most significant decisions facing the company while contributing directly to the development of projects and partnerships that support the future of sustainable aviation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Chief Investment Officer, you will be responsible for strengthening investment decision-making and value creation across SkyNRG.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead SkyNRG's Investment Management capability and establish the frameworks, governance and standards that support disciplined decision-making.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Further improve SkyNRG’s investment strategy, building on 17 years of SAF experience, network and track record, and the company’s overall strategic plans</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the evaluation and prioritization of major investments, strategic partnerships and growth opportunities across the portfolio.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring an institutional investor mindset into the organization, fostering collaboration across teams and ensuring opportunities are assessed through the lens of strategic fit, risk-adjusted returns and long-term value creation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide leadership to Corporate Development and Project Commercial activities, building high-performing teams and fostering a collaborative, results-driven culture that aligns strategic ambitions, commercial execution and investment outcomes.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the development of bankable, financeable and commercially attractive SAF projects.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead selected M&amp;A, partnership and corporate development opportunities that contribute to SkyNRG's long-term growth strategy.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted advisor to the CEO, Executive Committee, Board and shareholders on investment strategy, capital allocation and portfolio prioritization.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Areas of Impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Investment Strategy</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will provide leadership on how capital is allocated across SkyNRG's portfolio, ensuring resources are directed toward opportunities with the greatest strategic and commercial potential.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will oversee investment evaluations, valuation methodologies, business case development and portfolio prioritization to support informed decision-making at Executive Committee and Board level.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Portfolio Development</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will help maximize value across SkyNRG's portfolio by strengthening investment discipline throughout the project lifecycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From opportunity identification through commercial structuring and execution, you will ensure investment decisions are supported by robust analysis, clear governance and a strong understanding of risk and value drivers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partnerships</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth opportunities are expected to come from a combination of project development, strategic partnerships and selective corporate development initiatives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will play a leading role in identifying, assessing and executing opportunities that enhance SkyNRG's position within the sustainable aviation ecosystem and support the company's long-term ambitions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Organizational Leadership</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will collaborate closely with teams across Projects, Commercial, Finance, Legal and Strategy to strengthen how investment opportunities are evaluated and executed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By embedding a common investment framework across the business, you will increase transparency, improve decision quality and support a culture focused on value creation and accountability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we are looking for</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a strategic and collaborative leader with a strong track record in investment, infrastructure, energy or related capital-intensive industries. You are able to build trust across diverse stakeholder groups and bring people together around complex decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You combine strategic thinking with strong commercial judgment and have experience evaluating complex investment opportunities in capital-intensive environments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable influencing senior stakeholders, engaging with boards and shareholders and navigating situations where commercial, financial and strategic considerations intersect.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">15+ years of relevant experience in infrastructure, energy transition, project finance, private equity, corporate development or investment management.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of evaluating and executing complex investment opportunities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep expertise in valuation, financial analysis, capital allocation and investment decision-making.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with executive teams, Boards and institutional investors.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong leadership and stakeholder management capabilities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to balance strategic vision with pragmatic execution.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A genuine interest in accelerating the transition toward more sustainable aviation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We recognize that exceptional candidates may not meet every listed requirement. If you are excited about the opportunity to shape the future of sustainable aviation and believe your experience can contribute to our ambitions, we encourage you to apply.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location &amp; International Exposure</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based at SkyNRG's Amsterdam headquarters, this role offers the opportunity to work across an international network of partners, investors and project stakeholders that are helping shape the future of sustainable aviation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a flexible hybrid working model, recognizing that impactful leadership can be delivered through a combination of in-person collaboration, stakeholder engagement and remote working.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join SkyNRG</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an opportunity to play a defining role in one of the most dynamic and ambitious companies operating within the sustainable aviation sector.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Chief Investment Officer, you will influence investment decisions that shape the future of the company, contribute to the development of large-scale SAF projects and help create long-term value for shareholders, partners and the aviation industry as a whole.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join an entrepreneurial and mission-driven organization where commercial success and sustainable impact go hand in hand, and where your decisions will directly influence the growth trajectory of both the business and the broader SAF ecosystem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Is this you?</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to take the next step in your career with SkyNRG? Explore our vacancies and become part of our company of change makers. Together, we can change the future of flying.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information about SkyNRG visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.skynrg.com"><u>www.skynrg.com</u></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>📌 Please note: We do not accept sales inquiries or intermediary services.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At SkyNRG, we deeply value inclusion and diversity. As an equal opportunity employer, we are dedicated to ensuring every applicant has a fair chance, irrespective of race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, or any other legally protected characteristics.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skynrg/chief-investment-officer-cio-amsterdam-215904","tags":["Management"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793882432},{"slug":"people-business-partner-amsterdam-6150","company_name":"Mytomorrows","title":"People Business Partner","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About myTomorrows</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">myTomorrows is a global health tech company dedicated to breaking down barriers for patients seeking treatment options.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We strive to enable earlier and better treatment access by bridging the gap between those searching for possible options, and the companies who develop them. We work closely with patients, healthcare professionals, trial sites, patient advocacy groups, and BioPharma – connecting key stakeholders in the drug development ecosystem.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve developed a cutting-edge AI-powered technology platform that simplifies and streamlines access to drugs in development. To support our users and clients, we have a range of industry-expert specialized teams ready to help. Our services include clinical trial patient recruitment, Expanded Access Program management and Real-World Data collection.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With a global footprint spanning 134 countries, to date we’ve supported over 17,000 patients, 3,000 physicians and 350 sites, earning the trust of 60+ BioPharma companies. In October 2025, we closed a €25M investment with Avego Healthcare Capital to fuel our global ambitions and scale the business.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of treatment access - making tomorrow’s therapies accessible for people who need them today. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The opportunity: People Business Partner</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a People Business Partner at myTomorrows, you are a trusted advisor to senior leaders and the Leadership Team. In this Individual contributor People Business Partner role, you will translate business priorities into practical people solutions that enable high performing teams and organizational growth.<