pplication of People policies, employment legislation, and People practices across your business areas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead cross functional People projects that improve organizational effectiveness, manager capability, and operational excellence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted sparring partner who balances strategic thinking with hands on execution.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What you bring to the table:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 5 years of progressive HR experience or experience as a People Business Partner in a fast growing international organization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience partnering with senior leaders on organizational and people topics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive experience managing complex employee relations, performance management, and organizational change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong coaching, influencing, and stakeholder management skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid knowledge of Dutch employment law and HR best practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills with the ability to translate people data into actionable business insights.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable operating independently, making sound judgments, and managing competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a technology, SaaS, HealthTech, or scale up environment is highly preferred.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with modern HR systems such as Personio is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting international teams is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What we offer:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve a purposeful mission by helping patients gain access to potentially lifesaving treatments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">International work environment with scale up energy and a flat organization.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary, annual performance bonus, and equity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Great career development opportunities in a growing company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning and development budget alongside internal knowledge sharing sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attractive pension plan with the full premium covered by us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid working model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Policies that support working parents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthy lunch at the office.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited access to professional guidance by certified psychologists through OpenUp.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An additional holiday every year to celebrate Liberation Day on May 5.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal opportunities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">myTomorrows is an Equal Opportunity Employer and, beyond upholding discrimination-free practices, we are committed to cultivating a workplace where difference and diversity are protected and celebrated. The best work comes from our best selves, and we go to great lengths in supporting our team members to be just that. </p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/mytomorrows/people-business-partner-amsterdam-6150","tags":["People and Culture"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam HQ","created_at":1793882432},{"slug":"mandatory-internship-overall-aircraft-design-all-genders-delft-258390","company_name":"væridion","title":"Mandatory Internship Overall Aircraft Design (all genders)","description":"<h2><strong>Your Mission:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of aviation history at VÆRIDION, where we’re pioneering the world’s first electric nine-seater aircraft! As an <strong>Overall Aircraft Design Intern (all genders)</strong>, you will join our Central Engineering team and support across various Overall Aircraft Design activities. This role is a broad role, and you will perform different tasks to support on-going aircraft design and analysis activities. You will be part of our interdisciplinary aircraft design team and contribute directly to the design process of our battery-electric aircraft.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Your Day-to-Day:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the analysis and comparison of battery-electric aircraft concepts across different configurations and mission profiles.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investigate how technology assumptions and key design parameters influence aircraft performance, energy demand, and overall feasibility.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and adapt computational tools to support aircraft sizing, mission analysis, and design trade-off studies.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform parameter and sensitivity studies to explore design dependencies and identify key technology drivers.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collect, assess, and organise technical data to support consistent modelling assumptions and comparative analyses.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Document methods, assumptions, and results, and prepare clear visualisations to discuss findings with the engineering team.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your Profile:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Currently enrolled in a Master’s degree programme in Aerospace Engineering or a comparable technical discipline.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holding a Bachelor’s degree in Aerospace Engineering or a comparable technical discipline. </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent programming skills (e.g., Python, MATLAB).</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with aircraft design process, methods and tools. Experience with dedicated tools such as OpenMDAO and Aviary is a strong plus.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Readily available knowledge about aircraft. </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structured, analytical, and solution-oriented professional with strong ownership, facilitation, and stakeholder-management skills. </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English; additional European languages are an asset, combined with a strong motivation for aviation and electric aircraft technologies.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We recognize that women and other under-represented groups are often overlooked in our industry. If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every listed qualification, we still encourage you to apply. Talent and potential can’t always be captured in a checklist.</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Why us?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of an ambitious team determined to shape the future of aviation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an in-office company, but we value flexibility and trust employees to manage their schedules responsibly. This may include occasional remote work 